# Sending Invoices Section
KSEF_SendingInvoices=Sending invoices
KSEF_TheWorkflow=The Workflow
KSEF_Workflow_Step1=Create or open an invoice
KSEF_Workflow_Step2=Add fields as needed
KSEF_Workflow_Step3=Click the KSeF button
KSEF_Workflow_Step4=Wait for confirmation

KSEF_ValidateAndUpload_Desc=On draft invoices, handles validation and upload in one step. Can be hidden in settings if you prefer the payment-first workflow below
KSEF_UploadToKSEF_Desc=On validated, paid, or closed invoices, uploads to KSeF

KSEF_HowTo_Sending_PaymentFirst=Payment-First Workflow
KSEF_HowTo_Sending_PaymentFirstDesc=If you want payment data included in the KSeF XML: validate the invoice first, record payment(s), then click "Send to KSeF". The XML will include payment status, date, and amount. To encourage this flow, disable the "Validate and send to KSeF" button on the Outgoing: Sending settings tab. This removes the one-click shortcut so the separate steps are more obvious.

KSEF_Statuses=Statuses
KSEF_STATUS_ACCEPTED_Desc=Invoice received a KSeF number, you're done
KSEF_STATUS_PENDING_Desc=Still processing, check back shortly
KSEF_STATUS_REJECTED_Desc=Failed: see the error details and retry. Rejected by KSeF: not retried, fix the invoice (Modify) and send again; a rejected offline invoice gets a Technical Correction
KSEF_STATUS_OFFLINE_Desc=Issued offline after KSeF could not be reached. The scheduled job uploads it as soon as KSeF answers; the upload deadline is shown on the invoice

KSEF_ForeignCurrencyInvoices=Foreign Currency Invoices
KSEF_ForeignCurrencyDesc=For invoices in EUR or other non-PLN currencies the Multicurrency module must be enabled and the NBP rate fetched before sending (Fetch NBP Rate on the invoice card). The rate comes from the last NBP table before the earlier of the invoice date and the sale date (VAT Act art. 31a); a deposit invoice paid before its date uses the table before the payment; an intra-EU supply (all lines WDT 0 %%) uses the invoice date, but no later than the 15th of the month after the delivery (a WDT deposit invoice uses its invoice date); corrections keep the rate of the invoice they correct. Settings ("NBP rate date") can switch to the income tax rule instead (VAT Act art. 31a ust. 2a): the table before the day revenue arises (the sale date, or the earlier invoice date or full payment), intra-EU supplies included; deposit invoices stay on the VAT rule. The choice binds for at least 12 months. If a date changes after the rate was fetched, the rate no longer fits: the card shows it in amber and sending is refused until it is fetched again (invoices validated before the upgrade only get a warning). In settings you choose whether a new rate changes the PLN or the foreign currency amount, similar to multicurrency.

KSEF_BankAccountOnInvoice=Bank Account on Invoices
KSEF_BankAccountOnInvoiceDesc=If you send invoices with bank transfer as the payment method and want your bank account details (IBAN) to appear on the invoice, you need to assign a bank account to the invoice. Dolibarr can auto-fill this for you.
KSEF_BankAccount_Step1=Go to Bank/Cash and make sure your bank account has the IBAN filled in (SWIFT/BIC and bank name are optional but recommended)
KSEF_BankAccount_Step2=Go to the customer's Third Party card and set a default bank account - this will auto-fill on new invoices for that customer
KSEF_BankAccount_Step3=When creating an invoice with wire transfer payment, verify the Bank Account dropdown shows the correct account
KSEF_BankAccount_Step4=If the bank account is set and payment method is wire transfer, the IBAN will be included in the KSeF XML automatically

KSEF_AfterAcceptance=After Acceptance
KSEF_AfterAcceptanceDesc=Once accepted, you can generate a KSeF-style PDF visualization from the invoice card. If you have QR codes enabled in settings, the KSeF number also gets added to your regular invoice PDFs.

KSEF_CheckingStatusDesc=The KSeF tab on any invoice card shows all submission attempts for that invoice. The Outgoing invoices page lists every invoice with its latest send, its match with KSeF and the common errors:

