KSEF_CustomerExclusions=Customers left out of sending
KSEF_CustomerExclusionsDesc=Some customers don't need invoices sent to KSeF. You can exclude specific customers either from the module settings page or directly on the third party card using the exclusion checkbox.

# Troubleshooting Section
KSEF_Troubleshooting=Troubleshooting
KSEF_FindingErrorDetails=Finding Error Details
KSEF_FindingErrorDetailsDesc=Open the invoice, go to the KSeF tab, and view the error code and message. The Outgoing invoices page also shows the common errors (Common errors box):
KSEF_ConfigureNow=Configure now

KSEF_CommonIssues=Common Issues

KSEF_Issue_DuplicateNumber=Duplicate invoice number (Error 440)
KSEF_Issue_DuplicateNumber_Desc=KSeF already holds an invoice with this number. If it is this invoice (e.g. an earlier send whose answer was lost), the module takes the KSeF number over by itself, or use "Link KSeF number" on the card. If it is a different invoice (common in TEST / DEMO, where data persists), change the invoice number and send again. A duplicate is never retried as is.

KSEF_Issue_AuthFailed_Desc=First, verify your token or certificate hasn't expired. If credentials are valid, the most common cause is missing permissions in the KSeF portal. Go to "Moje uprawnienia" in the KSeF application and verify you have upload/download permissions configured. Valid authentication alone isn't sufficient - permissions must be explicitly assigned.

KSEF_Issue_NBPMissing=NBP rate missing
KSEF_Issue_NBPMissing_Desc=Foreign currency invoice without a fitting exchange rate. Use Fetch NBP Rate on the invoice card, and fetch it again after changing the invoice or sale date.

KSEF_Issue_Timeout_Desc=KSeF did not answer in time. The default limit is 7 seconds. The submission may still have reached KSeF: use Check status first, and send again only if it did not arrive.

KSEF_RetryLimits=Retry Limits
KSEF_RetryLimitsDesc=Every attempt is kept on the invoice's KSeF tab. A failed send can be retried from the card or the Outgoing invoices page; the scheduled job keeps checking open sends. Not retried: an invoice KSeF rejected (fix it and send again), a rejected offline invoice (Technical Correction), an unknown outcome with a KSeF reference (Check status first).


