KSEF_RefreshNBPRate=Refresh
KSEF_FetchNBPRate=Fetch NBP rate
KSEF_RefreshNBPRateTooltip=Fetch latest NBP exchange rate for this invoice date
KSEF_NBPRateKeepOriginal=Keep the original invoice's rate
KSEF_NBPRateCorrectOriginal=Correct the original's wrong rate: NBP table %s of %s
KSEF_NBPRateCorrectionChoiceTooltip=The original invoice's stored NBP table does not match its date under the current rate date rule. A correction keeps the rate the original invoice used. Pick the NBP table of the original's date only to correct a wrong rate on the original: the foreign amounts stay, the PLN amounts and the PLN VAT difference follow the corrected rate.
KSEF_NBPRateCorrectionTyped=This corrective invoice has the exchange rate %s, which is neither the rate of the corrected invoice %s (%s) nor the rate of the NBP table for the corrected invoice's date, %s (table date in brackets). A corrective invoice converts at the corrected invoice's rate; another rate is right only to correct a wrong rate on the corrected invoice.
KSEF_NBPRateCorrectionTypedDraftHint=To change it, set the corrective invoice back to draft first.
KSEF_NBPRateCreditNoteTyped=This credit note has the exchange rate %s, which is neither the rate of the original invoice %s (%s) nor the rate of the NBP table for the original invoice's date, %s (table date in brackets). A credit note converts at the original invoice's rate; another rate is right only to correct a wrong rate on the original invoice.
KSEF_NBPRateCreditNoteTypedDraftHint=To change it, set the credit note back to draft first.
KSEF_NBPRateTypedHintBoth=On the draft, use the "Correct the original's wrong rate" button next to the NBP rate (or "Keep the original invoice's rate"): it sets the rate and the NBP table date together.
KSEF_NBPRateTypedHintKeep=On the draft, use the "Keep the original invoice's rate" button next to the NBP rate: it sets the rate and the NBP table date together.
KSEF_NBPRateKorektaSettled=The NBP rate of corrective invoice %s cannot be changed now: the new rate changes its PLN amounts, and it already has: %s. Those amounts would not be recalculated. Set it back to draft (remove its payments first), pick the rate and validate it again.
KSEF_NBPRateSettledPayments=payments
KSEF_NBPRateSettledCredits=a settlement with the corrected invoice (credits and discounts)
KSEF_NBPRateBooked=The NBP rate of invoice %s cannot be changed: the new rate changes its amounts, and Dolibarr no longer allows modifying the invoice (%s). To correct the rate, issue a corrective invoice.
