KSEF_HintSettlementCorrection=A deposit this invoice settles changed after the invoice was sent to KSeF (payment or correction). The corrective invoice starts with the deposit at its current value; check it, then validate and send it.
KSEF_SettlementNeedsKorRoz=Deposit invoice %s changed after this invoice was sent (payment or correction). Issue a correction. This invoice deducts %s; the deposit is now worth %s.
KSEF_DepositSettlementNeedsKorRoz=Settlement invoice %s, already sent to KSeF, deducts this deposit as it was before it changed (payment or correction): %s instead of %s. Issue a settlement corrective invoice for it.
KSEF_SettlementCorrectionPrefilled=This correction settles deposit invoice %s at its new value: %s instead of %s. Check it, then validate and send it.
KSEF_SettlementCorrectionRateMissing=Deposit invoice %s now also has VAT rate %s, which this correction does not deduct, and the deposit has other unused credit. Apply the credit of that rate to the correction that settles it, then validate and send it.
KSEF_SettlementCorrectionRateMissingAtValidate=Deposit invoice %s gained VAT rate %s after this correction was drafted, and this correction does not deduct it. The credit of that rate stays unused: apply it to the invoice or correction that settles it.
KSEF_SettlementCorrectionRefreshed=Deposit invoice %s changed after this correction was drafted: the deposit amount was updated to its current value, %s instead of %s. Check the amount left to pay before you send it.
