KSEF_CorrectionStockUndoSkipped=%s back to draft: negative stock is not allowed, so Dolibarr did not take the correction's goods out of stock for %s. The stock was left as is: for that quantity the module did not put the corrected invoice's goods back (the quantities backed out when the correction was validated stay backed out). Check the stock (and the product's average price) and correct it by hand if needed.
KSEF_CorrectionStockUndoNoCore=%s: Dolibarr did not reverse the correction's own stock movement for %s (no warehouse chosen, stock change on invoice validation turned off, or a product with lots). For that quantity the module did not move the corrected invoice's goods back either (the quantities backed out when the correction was validated stay backed out). Check the stock (and the product's average price) and correct it by hand if needed.
KSEF_CorrectionStockUndoShort=%s: negative stock is not allowed, so the module did not take all of the corrected invoice's goods back out of stock (you chose to go on anyway). The stock no longer matches the documents: %s. Correct it by hand (stock correction).
KSEF_CorrectionStockUndoShortRefused=%s: negative stock is not allowed and the warehouse no longer holds enough of the goods the correction put back to stock (sold again since), so undoing the correction's stock change would leave the stock wrong: %s. Refused. Add the missing goods to stock (a reception or a stock correction) first, then try again; on the invoice card you can also go on anyway.
KSEF_CorrectionStockShortRow=%s (%s): should be %s, ends at %s
