KSEF_HowTo_Corrections=Corrective invoices
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_Intro=Polish tax law uses one concept for all invoice corrections: <b>faktura korygująca</b>. In the module it is the <b>Corrective invoice</b>, sent to KSeF referencing the original invoice, which must be in KSeF first.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_WhenTitle=When to use which type
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_CreditNote=<b>Credit note</b> (Dolibarr): a negative invoice that can only reduce amounts. <b>Corrective invoice</b> is recommended, as it handles any change.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_Replacement=<b>Corrective invoice</b> corrects the original as a whole. Use for any change: amounts, VAT rates, addresses, or lines. Paid invoices can also be corrected this way.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_CreateTitle=Creating a correction
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_CreateButton=After an invoice is accepted in KSeF, a <b>Corrective invoice</b> button appears on the invoice card. It opens the creation page with the correction type and source invoice pre-selected. Dolibarr's own credit note button is labelled <b>Credit note</b> on the card: it can only reduce amounts.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_CreateRadio=Corrections can also be created from the invoice creation page by selecting the corrective invoice radio and choosing the source invoice.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_PaidInvoice=For paid invoices, a discount is automatically applied to settle the correction when validated. The original invoice is restored to Paid/Closed status (not canceled).
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_DetailsTitle=Correction details
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_Reason=<b>Correction Reason</b> - free-text reason for the correction. Recommended by Polish tax law but not required by the KSeF schema. Choose from preset reasons or enter custom text. Always stored in Polish. A default can be set on the Outgoing: Sending tab.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_Type=<b>Correction Type</b> - when the correction takes effect: original invoice date, corrective invoice date, or another date. Optional.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_KsefTitle=What gets sent to KSeF
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_KsefXml=The corrective invoice XML references the original by its KSeF number. Line method is configurable on the Outgoing: Sending tab:
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_MethodDiff=<b>Differential</b> - only delta lines showing the change
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_MethodStan=<b>Before/After</b> (state before, default) - original and corrected state for each line
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_CreditNoteDiff=Credit notes always use the Differential method regardless of this setting.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ChainTitle=Correction chains
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_Chain=A corrective invoice can itself be corrected (korekta korekty). Each correction in the chain references the previous one. You cannot unvalidate or delete an invoice that has been corrected.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ConfigTitle=Configuration
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_Config=Correction settings are on the <b>Outgoing: Sending</b> settings tab under <b>Corrective Invoices</b>: default correction reason and correction line method (Differential / Before-After).
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits=Deposit and settlement (final) invoices
KSEF_HowTo_DepositsDesc=Deposits for an order are invoiced as deposit invoices and settled by the settlement invoice (sometimes called final invoice). There is no separate invoice type: the settlement invoice is a standard invoice with the deposits applied. Use the normal Dolibarr flow; the module picks the KSeF type itself and shows it on the invoice card in the row "KSeF invoice type".
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Step1=Create and validate the customer order (or proposal).
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Step2=On the order: Create invoice, type <strong>Deposit invoice</strong>, a percentage of the order (or a fixed amount, see the rules below). Validate it and send it to KSeF: it goes out as a deposit invoice with the order's value and lines.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Step3=When the customer pays: Enter payment on the deposit invoice, then <strong>Mark as credit available</strong>.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Step4=Further deposits work the same way. The deposit that completes the order lists the earlier ones in KSeF by itself.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Step5=After delivery: on the order, Create invoice, type <strong>Standard invoice</strong> (all order lines).
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Step6=On this draft, apply every available deposit credit (Dolibarr lists one per VAT rate; apply each one). The amount to pay drops by the deposits.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Step7=Validate and send: it goes out as a settlement invoice with the full order lines, the remaining amount and the KSeF numbers of the deposits.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_FullTitle=Deposits cover everything
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Full=If the deposits cover the whole order, the settlement invoice is optional. If you issue it, it is sent as a settlement with nothing to pay, as the Ministry of Finance manual describes.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_RulesTitle=Rules
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule1=Send every deposit to KSeF before its settlement invoice: a settlement invoice whose deposit is not in KSeF is refused, with a link to that deposit. A deposit sent outside the module (e.g. in the MF app) is linked first with "Link KSeF number" on its card. The current KSeF environment counts: a deposit accepted only in the Test or Demo environment must also be sent in Production before a settlement invoice sent in Production can cite it.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule2=Link the deposit to its order or proposal (create it from the order): without it KSeF does not get the order value.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule3=A <strong>fixed amount</strong> deposit made from an order or a proposal is split across the order's VAT rates in proportion to their gross amounts (as Dolibarr does with its setting MAIN_DEPOSIT_MULTI_TVA). A deposit with a rate its order does not have is refused at sending.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule4=Corrections: correct a deposit or settlement invoice with Corrective invoice (a Credit note only decreases); the module sends the right kind of corrective invoice. The deposit's credit follows its new value as far as it was paid (payments stay where they were), and a settlement invoice not sent yet follows it too. A deposit that changes after its settlement invoice was sent (a correction, or a payment that changes its credit) leaves that invoice with a warning and the Settlement corrective invoice button, which makes the corrective invoice with the deposit at its current value; a settlement corrective invoice still in draft is updated to the deposit's current value when you validate it.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule5=Foreign currency: each deposit uses its own NBP rate; the settlement invoice states the VAT left to pay in PLN at its own rate.


KSEF_HowTo_AdvancedFields=Advanced FA(3) Fields
KSEF_HowTo_AdvancedFields_Intro=Optional fields that add extra data to the FA(3) XML. Configured on the <b>Outgoing: Fields</b> tab, except the seller EORI field which is on the <b>General</b> tab.
KSEF_HowTo_EntityFields=Entity Fields (Podmiot)
KSEF_HowTo_EntityFields_IDNabywcy=<b>Buyer ID</b> - stable buyer identifier used across corrections when buyer data changes. Source from customer code or a thirdparty extrafield. Optional.
KSEF_HowTo_EntityFields_EORI=<b>EORI Numbers</b> - EU customs/trade identifier. Set seller EORI in General settings. Buyer EORI reads the third party's professional-ID field mapped via the EORI field setting (General settings, default idprof5). Only relevant for EU customs operations.
KSEF_HowTo_LineFields=Line-Level Fields (invoice line)
KSEF_HowTo_LineFields_GTU=<b>GTU Markers</b> - goods/services classification (GTU_01 through GTU_13) per invoice line. Source from a product extrafield. Aids JPK_VAT alignment.
KSEF_HowTo_LineFields_Procedura=<b>Procedura Markers</b> - procedure codes per invoice line (WSTO_EE, IED, TT_D, MPP, etc.). Source from a product extrafield.
KSEF_HowTo_LineFields_UUID=<b>Line unique ID (UUID)</b> - unique identifier per invoice line for reliable line matching in corrections. Warning: visible on the KSeF PDF visualization, which may confuse recipients.
KSEF_HowTo_InvoiceFlags=Invoice Flags
KSEF_HowTo_InvoiceFlags_FP=<b>Invoice issued to a receipt</b> - invoice issued against a prior fiscal receipt. Set per invoice from an invoice extrafield in Outgoing settings (no POS auto-detect, since a POS issues real invoices too). Does not propagate to corrections.
KSEF_HowTo_InvoiceFlags_TP=<b>Related-party transaction</b> - the buyer is related to the seller (VAT Act art. 32 ust. 2 pkt 1). Read from a third-party or invoice extra field. The same marker goes into JPK_VAT.
KSEF_HowTo_InvoiceFlags_MPP=<b>MPP (split payment)</b> - set per invoice from an invoice extrafield. Prints the mandatory "Mechanizm podzielonej płatności" note on the PDF. <b>Inherits</b> onto corrective invoices. No accounting automation: seller-side MPP is just two partial payments (net to your regular account, VAT to the dedicated VAT account) you enter via each payment's bank account.
KSEF_HowTo_InvoiceFlags_P16=<b>Cash accounting (metoda kasowa)</b> - a taxpayer-level status, so normally set to "always on" in Outgoing settings.
KSEF_HowTo_InvoiceFlags_P17=<b>Self-billing (samofakturowanie)</b> - marks an invoice issued under the self-billing procedure. A per-document fact: set per invoice via an invoice extrafield, or as a per-customer default via a thirdparty extrafield. KSeF accepts it only when the buyer sends the invoice under its own self-billing permission; this module sends as the seller, so such an invoice is rejected (code 410).
KSEF_HowTo_InvoiceFlags_P18=<b>Reverse charge (odwrotne obciążenie)</b> - applies to cross-border / intra-EU reverse-charge supplies (Poland abolished domestic reverse charge in 2019). Any one source turns the flag on, so a per-invoice field cannot switch off a customer default: a per-customer default (thirdparty extrafield, e.g. an intra-EU customer always reverse-charged), a per-invoice extrafield, or always on. Intra-EU services not subject to Polish VAT (np II, art. 28b) set it automatically. A correction keeps the value the corrected invoice was sent with, unless it adds such a service.
# Third entity (#28)
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3=Third entity
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_Intro=FA(3) lets you declare an additional entity besides the seller and buyer, the "third entity" (podmiot trzeci). The most common case is a <b>payer (role 6)</b> who differs from the buyer, but it also covers an internal recipient unit, an additional buyer, an invoice issuer, JST/VAT-group members, and an employee. Enable it in <b>outgoing invoice settings</b>, then per invoice:
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_Step1=Enable <b>Third entity</b> in outgoing settings and pick a <b>default role</b> (overridable per invoice).
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_Step2=Open the <b>KSeF tab</b> of an invoice, and a third-entity picker appears. Choose the company and its role.
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_Step3=Save. The third entity is added to the FA(3) XML and shown on the KSeF PDF. Leave the company empty to add none. A corrective invoice sends its third entities again (the schema has no correction node for them): when it is created it takes those of the invoice it corrects, and you can change them on its card before sending.
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_Reconciliation=<b>Reconciliation is manual.</b> A payer's bank inflow is matched by hand against the buyer's receivable; the receivable stays on the buyer's sub-ledger (art. 356 KC). There is no accounting automation in this release.
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_JSTGV_Title=JST / VAT-group roles (7/8/9/10)
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_JSTGV=Selling as a local government unit or a VAT group: add the unit or member that issues the invoice as a third entity with role 7 or 9. Selling to one: add the receiving unit or member as a third entity with role 8 or 10, and tick <b>Local government unit (JST)</b> or <b>VAT group (GV)</b> on the customer card so the module warns before sending when that third entity is missing. Third entities must be turned on (Outgoing: Fields tab, "Third entity").
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_IDWew_Title=Internal identifier (branches / internal units / employees)
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_IDWew_What=<b>What is the internal identifier?</b> It is a code a company generates inside KSeF for one of its branches/establishments (zakład, oddział), internal units, or an employee treated as a separate unit. Its format is the company's NIP, a dash, then 5 digits, e.g. <b>1234567890-00001</b>. KSeF uses it for access permissions: people authorized for that unit can issue/see only invoices where the unit appears as the third entity. You normally need it when the third entity is an internal unit that has <b>no NIP of its own</b> (roles 2 and 11).
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_IDWew_How=<b>How to use it (optional):</b> create any <b>societe</b> extrafield (varchar/text) to hold the value, enter the internal ID on the third entity, then pick your field in outgoing settings in the <b>internal ID source</b> dropdown. The module then sends the internal ID instead of the NIP. Without a source picked (or with an empty value), the entity's own NIP (or a "no tax ID" marker for an employee with none) is used instead.
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_Limits_Title=Limitations in this release
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_Faktor=<b>Role 1 (Factor):</b> fully supported, including the factor's bank accounts - enter them on the third entity.
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_Role4=<b>Role 4 (additional buyer):</b> enter the co-buyer's share in the Share field (0-100%%); leave it blank for equal shares. On corrective invoices the co-buyer is sent as a new third entity rather than carried in the before-correction buyer block. This is enough for a single buyer; full correction linkage for several buyers is not supported yet.
KSEF_HowTo_Podmiot3_Subject3=<b>Purchase invoices naming you as a third entity:</b> the incoming invoice download asks KSeF only for invoices where your company is the seller or the buyer. An invoice addressed to your VAT group or JST that names your company only as a third entity (e.g. role 10 / 8) is not downloaded in this release; enter it by hand. On imported purchase invoices the third entities and the GV / JST markers stay in the stored KSeF XML (incoming invoice card, KSeF PDF); the supplier invoice has no field for them.

