KSEF_NotFoundInKsefComplete=Not found in KSeF: none of the %s KSeF sessions opened around the send on %s holds this invoice, so the search has stopped. Send it again with "Retry sending": if KSeF has it after all, its number is taken over, no second invoice.
KSEF_NotFoundInKsefExpired=Not found in KSeF: no match in the %s KSeF sessions searched, and more than %s days have passed since the send on %s, so the search has stopped. Send it again with "Retry sending": if KSeF has it after all, its number is taken over, no second invoice.
KSEF_NotFoundInKsefNoSession=Not found in KSeF: KSeF lists no session opened around the send on %s, so the invoice never reached it and the search has stopped. Send it again with "Retry sending": if KSeF has it after all, its number is taken over, no second invoice.
KSEF_ReplacedByAcceptedNote=KSeF holds this invoice under number %s from a later send, so this send is closed.
KSEF_HashStopInSales=Search stopped: KSeF holds exactly this invoice file under number %s (shown in Outgoing invoices), but the module could not confirm on its own that it belongs to this invoice, so the send stays open. Open that invoice in Outgoing invoices and check which Dolibarr invoice it is tied to; if it is this one, link them. Do not send again before checking: if the invoice number changed after the send, KSeF would take it a second time.
KSEF_HashStopInSalesNoRow=Search stopped: the Outgoing invoices sync found exactly this invoice file in KSeF, but the module could not confirm on its own that it belongs to this invoice, so the send stays open. Run the Outgoing invoices sync, find that invoice and, if it is the same one, link them. Do not send again before checking.
KSEF_HashStopAmbiguous=Search stopped: this invoice file is in %s KSeF sessions, so the module did not pick a number on its own and the send stays open. Send it again with "Retry sending": KSeF does not take a second invoice with the same number, and the module checks the copy KSeF holds and takes its number over.
KSEF_HashStopOpenSales=Open in Outgoing invoices
KSEF_HeldByDuplicate=A later send of this invoice was refused because KSeF already holds an invoice with this number (KSeF number %s). Most likely it is this send, so it is not closed. On the invoice card use "Link KSeF number": the module checks the copy in KSeF and, if it is this invoice, records its number.
KSEF_HeldByDuplicateNoNumber=A later send of this invoice was refused because KSeF already holds an invoice with this number. Most likely it is this send, so it is not closed. KSeF did not name the number: find the invoice with the Outgoing invoices sync and link it there.
KSEF_NotFoundInKsefOtherHolds=Not found in KSeF: a later send was refused as a duplicate, and the invoice KSeF holds under number %s is none of the files sent for this invoice. KSeF takes only one invoice with this number, so this send is not there. Follow the steps on the invoice card.
KSEF_HowTo_HashSearch=A send KSeF never answered
KSEF_HowTo_HashSearchDesc=If a send stopped before KSeF answered, the module looks for the invoice in KSeF by the hash of its file: on "Check status" and in the scheduled job, less and less often, for at most 7 days after the send. The statuses you may see:
KSEF_HowTo_HashSearch_Searching=the module is still looking for the invoice in KSeF. "Check status" searches the next sessions at once. "Retry sending" is safe: if KSeF already has the invoice, the module takes its number over instead of sending a second one.
KSEF_HowTo_HashSearch_NotFound=the search went through every KSeF session from the time of the send, or 7 days have passed, and the invoice was not found. Send it again with "Retry sending".
KSEF_HowTo_HashSearch_Replaced=a later send of this invoice was accepted, so this one is closed. Nothing to do; it shows only in the history on the KSeF tab.
KSEF_HowTo_HashSearch_InSales=KSeF holds exactly this invoice file, but the module could not confirm on its own that it belongs to this invoice. Open it in Outgoing invoices (the link is on the invoice card) and, if it is the same invoice, link them. Do not send again before checking.
KSEF_HowTo_HashSearch_Ambiguous=the invoice file is in several KSeF sessions. Use "Retry sending": KSeF does not take a second invoice with this number, and the module takes over the number KSeF holds.
KSEF_HowTo_HashSearch_Held=a later send was refused because KSeF already holds an invoice with this number, most likely from this send. Use "Link KSeF number" on the invoice card; it shows only in the history on the KSeF tab.
KSEF_TimeoutNoRefHint=No answer from KSeF and no KSeF reference: KSeF probably did not get it. Send again (a duplicate takes the KSeF number over) or mark as not sent.
KSEF_DupNextNotFound=KSeF does not show that number now: try "Link KSeF number" again later, or check the number in the KSeF portal
KSEF_DupNextNotOurs=The KSeF invoice with this number has different content: if it is this invoice (sent before a change), use "Link KSeF number"; if it is another invoice, give this one a new number
KSEF_DupNextNoPermission=The KSeF token cannot read invoices (InvoiceRead): grant it, then use "Link KSeF number"
