KSEF_CorrectionNoSource=This correction does not name the invoice it corrects, so it will not be sent to KSeF: a corrective invoice must carry the data of the corrected invoice (art. 106j(2) of the VAT Act). Open the original invoice and create the correction with "Corrective invoice".
KSEF_EarlierCorrectionUnsent=Send the earlier correction %s to KSeF first: this correction states the amounts after it
KSEF_KorZalRateMismatch=A corrective invoice of deposit invoice %s uses the deposit invoice's exchange rate %s, but this corrective invoice has %s. Set it back to draft and validate it again: validation sets the rate back to the deposit invoice's rate and recalculates the PLN amounts. Then send it again. Fetching the NBP rate does not help here: a corrective invoice of a deposit invoice keeps the deposit invoice's rate.
KSEF_KorZalRateRestored=Corrective invoice %s of deposit invoice %s: the exchange rate %s was set back to the deposit invoice's rate %s and the PLN amounts were recalculated (the foreign currency amounts stay). A corrective invoice of a deposit invoice converts at the deposit invoice's rate (art. 31b ust. 1 of the VAT Act), so Dolibarr shows the same PLN amounts as the invoice sent to KSeF.
KSEF_KorZalRateWillRestore=This corrective invoice of deposit invoice %s has the exchange rate %s, the deposit invoice %s. At validation the rate is set back to the deposit invoice's rate and the PLN amounts are recalculated: a corrective invoice of a deposit invoice converts at the deposit invoice's rate (art. 31b ust. 1 of the VAT Act).
KSEF_SupplierPaymentDeleteUnknown=The deleted supplier payment could not be traced to its invoices, so the credit of supplier deposits deducted on validated invoices was not rechecked. Run the Database check on the About tab of the KSeF settings to find deposit credits that no longer match.
