KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule6=Apply every deposit credit (Dolibarr makes one per VAT rate). A partly applied deposit, or an order deposit the invoice does not use, must be confirmed on each send with the tick "I checked the deposits, send this invoice anyway"; retries from the Outgoing invoices page and the scheduled job skip such invoices.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule7=Order changed after a deposit: the deposit's corrective invoice states the order before and after.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule8=Never abandon a deposit sent to KSeF: correct it with a corrective invoice.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule9=A deposit applied on the order (instead of the invoice) is recognised too: the invoice made from that order takes over the deposit's credit and is a settlement invoice, and the credit cannot be used a second time.
KSEF_HowTo_Deposits_Rule10=Deposits above the sale: a settlement invoice with a negative total is refused. Refunding a deposit needs a correction of the deposit invoice (the Corrective invoice button). A negative amount at one VAT rate (a deposit at a rate the invoice does not have) needs a confirmation at sending; better correct the deposit's rate or add a line at that rate.
KSEF_HowTo_ReconcileTitle=Matching your sales invoices with KSeF
KSEF_HowTo_ReconcileDesc=The Outgoing invoices page shows one row per invoice: its latest send and its match with KSeF. The "Sync Now" button (here, on the incoming list or on the KSeF dashboard) fetches sales and purchase invoices from KSeF and compares the sales with Dolibarr; the scheduled job does the same. Match states: OK, Differs (Match to KSeF), Not linked (Link), Not in Dolibarr (Import to Dolibarr), Missing in KSeF, Not sent or Optional (consumer / foreign).
KSEF_HowTo_ReconcileImport="Import to Dolibarr" creates a validated customer invoice from the KSeF XML, to rebuild invoices that are in KSeF but missing in Dolibarr.
KSEF_HowTo_ReconcileUpo=The sync also rebuilds missing UPOs in the background: from the KSeF session list it finds the session of each invoice that has a KSeF number but no UPO (e.g. after Import to Dolibarr), a few at a time within the KSeF limits. A token with only the invoice-sending right sees only the sessions it opened itself; a token with Introspection sees them all.
KSEF_HowTo_ReconcileReset=Admin options: "Reset sync position" keeps the stored invoices and fetches everything again; a completeness check then reports how many missing invoices were found. A deleted record does not come back on the next sync, only after a reset.
KSEF_HowTo_Rights=Dolibarr user rights
KSEF_HowTo_RightsDesc=Viewing KSeF data needs <b>KSeF: read</b>. Sending to KSeF needs <b>KSeF: create/update</b> and <b>Invoices: create</b> (with advanced permissions, "Validate and send to KSeF" also needs <b>Invoices: validate</b>). A button the user may not use is shown greyed with the missing right. When the module is re-enabled after an upgrade from an older version, every user and group with Invoices: create gets KSeF: create/update once; remove it where it is not wanted, it is not granted again.
KSEF_HowTo_EnvFilter=Lists and the dashboard show only the current environment. When another environment also has records, a note above the Outgoing and Incoming invoice lists says so; to see them, switch the environment on the Authentication tab.
KSEF_STATUS_TIMEOUT_Desc=Sent, but KSeF gave no final answer. Use "Check status"; the invoice is sent again only if KSeF did not receive it
KSEF_STATUS_INTERRUPTED_Desc=The send stopped before KSeF answered and KSeF gave it no reference number, so there is nothing to check. Use "Retry sending" (if KSeF took it after all, the duplicate takes its number over) or mark it as not sent
KSEF_HowTo_Offline=Offline mode
KSEF_HowTo_OfflineDesc=Offline invoices (emergency mode) need the Offline certificate (Authentication tab). The module never switches to offline on its own:
KSEF_HowTo_Offline1=Offline is offered only after a send failed because KSeF could not be reached (never after a rejection), or for a backdated invoice. Without the Offline certificate the option is greyed.
KSEF_HowTo_Offline2=An offline invoice carries two QR codes. The scheduled job uploads it as soon as KSeF answers; a backdated one is uploaded at once. "Send to KSeF" on the card uploads it by hand.
KSEF_HowTo_Offline3=Past the upload deadline it stays sendable and is marked "Overdue": send it without delay.
KSEF_HowTo_Offline4=If KSeF rejects an uploaded offline invoice, send a Technical Correction from the card; the same XML is never sent again.
KSEF_HowTo_Offline5=A server error from KSeF (for example 502 or 504) can arrive after KSeF has already accepted the invoice. Before issuing offline after such an error, check the status first. If the invoice turns out to be in KSeF twice, issue a correction to zero for the duplicate.
KSEF_HowTo_OfflineWhen=When: only while KSeF is unavailable (an outage, a break announced by the Ministry of Finance, no connection) or when the invoice's issue date is earlier than the day it is sent. In every other case send it with the usual "Send to KSeF".
KSEF_HowTo_OfflineTest=Offline mode cannot be tried from Dolibarr on the Test environment: KSeF Test answers, so no outage can be caused, and without an Offline certificate for Test the "Issue Offline Invoice" button is greyed.
KSEF_HowTo_OfflineDo=What to do: upload the Offline certificate for the environment you issue invoices in (Authentication tab, "Set up Offline certificate"). When a send fails because KSeF does not answer, click "Issue Offline Invoice" on the invoice card and give the customer the invoice with its two QR codes. The module sends it to KSeF by itself once KSeF answers again; keep an eye on the upload deadline in the KSeF status row.
KSEF_HowTo_EditSent=Changing a sent invoice
KSEF_HowTo_EditSentDesc=In Production an invoice accepted by KSeF or issued offline cannot go back to draft: change it with a corrective invoice (offline: a Technical Correction or a corrective invoice). In Test and Demo going back to draft is allowed with a warning; the change does not reach KSeF. A copy of an invoice (clone, replacement, invoice from an order) does not take over the KSeF number, status or send date; a clone also needs a new NBP rate.
KSEF_HowTo_NumberNoRecord=KSeF number without a send record
KSEF_HowTo_NumberNoRecordDesc=If an invoice has a KSeF number but no send record (typed in by hand, or the record was lost), the card offers "Link KSeF number": the number is checked against KSeF and recorded. Sending again asks for confirmation first, because it creates a second invoice in KSeF.
KSEF_HowTo_DbCheckDesc=On the About tab, admins can run the check of the module database: tables, fields, keys, jobs and records. The check itself changes nothing. Fixes come in three steps, each shown only when needed: 1. "Repair" adds what is missing and changes no records; 2. "Correct records" first lists the changes (of repeated records the one accepted in KSeF or already imported into Dolibarr stays, or else the newest; links to deleted records are emptied; an unknown status becomes "Error"), and one button undoes it until the next send or import; 3. under "Advanced" a table can be rebuilt, with its records back from a backup. The same section lists invoices with a KSeF number but no module record (open the invoice and use "Link KSeF number") and shows an error when the database does not save module data. Notes about single invoices are on the invoice card. With Multicompany only the superadmin may repair or rebuild. A backup of the module tables is made automatically before Repair, Correct records, a rebuild, Apply update and Restore (the last 10 are kept); "Backups of the module tables" lists them for download, restore (with a tick confirming the data is replaced) or upload of a file downloaded earlier, e.g. on a new server. They hold only the module tables: make a full Dolibarr backup too (Home > Admin tools > Backup).
