# REST API
KSEF_RestUpoNeedsRecovery=No KSeF session reference is stored for this invoice (number tied by hand or taken over), so KSeF cannot be asked for its UPO directly; waiting will not help. Use "Download UPO" on the invoice (it searches KSeF for the session), or download the UPO from the KSeF taxpayer application.
KSEF_HowTo_RestTitle=REST API
KSEF_HowTo_RestIntro=Other programs can use the module through the Dolibarr REST API. Every request sends the API key of a Dolibarr user in the <b>DOLAPIKEY</b> header and has that user's rights. Base address (the older <b>/api/index.php/ksef/</b> worked only up to Dolibarr 23):
KSEF_HowTo_RestSetup=Setup: enable the Dolibarr module "API REST", generate an API key on the user's card, and when the constant API_ENDPOINT_RULES is set, allow <b>ksefapi:1</b>. The API explorer lists every route with its parameters:
KSEF_HowTo_RestRights=Rights: reading needs <b>Read KSeF submissions and incoming invoices</b> and <b>Read customer invoices (and payments)</b>; lists and counts show only the invoices the user may see (an external user: their own company; a sales representative without "Extend access to all third parties AND their objects...": their own customers). Sending (submit, submit-offline, retry, link) needs <b>Send to KSeF and manage KSeF records</b> and <b>Create/modify customer invoices</b>.
KSEF_HowTo_RestCodes=Answers: 200 done; 400 wrong parameter; 403 missing right; 404 not found; 409 the state does not allow it now (error.status says why: act, then call again); 422 KSeF rejected the invoice or it cannot be built (error.ksef_code); 429 KSeF limit (error.retry_after); 500 server error (details in the Dolibarr log); 502 NBP rate not available; 503 KSeF not reachable, try later. The README (REST API section) lists every status.
