KSEF_FA3_INCLUDE_WZ_Help=Write the references of the validated shipments the invoice was created from as WZ numbers. Shipments only linked to the invoice's order are not used. Off by default.
KSEF_FA3_LINE_DATES=Line supply dates
KSEF_FA3_LINE_DATES_Help=Automatic: when every line has the same service period (start before end), the invoice states it as the invoice period instead of the sale date; when the lines carry different dates (end date, else start date), each line gets its own delivery date and lines without a date get the sale date. On an invoice in another currency, a line whose date has another NBP rate than the invoice is converted at its own rate (VAT Act art. 31a). Corrections keep the sale date. Off by default.
KSEF_FA3_LINE_DATES_disabled=Disabled (sale date only)
KSEF_FA3_LINE_DATES_auto=Automatic from the line dates
KSEF_FA3_PERIOD_FIELDS=Invoice period fields
KSEF_FA3_PERIOD_FIELDS_Help=Shows the fields "Invoice period from / to (KSeF)" on invoices. When both are filled, the invoice states this period instead of the sale date, overriding the line dates. Off by default.
KSEF_FA3_ORDER_DATE_FIELD=Order date field
KSEF_FA3_ORDER_DATE_FIELD_Help=Shows the field "Order date (KSeF)" on invoices. When filled, it is written as the order date of every order number that has no date of its own, whatever the order number source. A linked order always brings its own date. Off by default.
KSEF_NR_ZAMOWIENIA_PARSE_DATE=Parse date from order number field
KSEF_NR_ZAMOWIENIA_PARSE_DATE_Help=Only for the invoice field source: a date at the start of the field (day/month/year, e.g. "02.02.2026 12/2026") becomes the order date and is removed from the number. Dates outside 1990-2050 are ignored.
KSEF_FA3_INCLUDE_LINE_VAT=VAT amount of each line
KSEF_FA3_INCLUDE_LINE_VAT_Help=The VAT for each rate may be the sum of the lines' VAT amounts only when those amounts are shown on the invoice (VAT Act art. 106e ust. 10). Otherwise it is calculated from the net total of that rate (art. 106e ust. 1 pkt 14). With the first option, the lines' VAT amounts are shown only on invoices where their sum differs from the VAT calculated from the net total. With the second, they are shown on every line. If you do not want them on your invoices, switch on the Dolibarr rounding mode that calculates the VAT from each rate's total (MAIN_ROUNDOFTOTAL_NOT_TOTALOFROUND = 1): the lines then add up to the same VAT, so the first option shows no line amounts. They are never shown on lines with the gross method, the margin scheme, or a 0%%, exempt or not-taxed rate.
KSEF_FA3_INCLUDE_LINE_VAT_auto=Only when the lines add up to a different VAT (recommended)
KSEF_FA3_INCLUDE_LINE_VAT_1=Always
KSEF_FX_PLN_VAT_METHOD=PLN VAT on invoices in another currency
KSEF_FX_PLN_VAT_METHOD_Help=On an invoice in another currency only the VAT has to be shown in PLN (VAT Act art. 106e ust. 11). The law does not say whether the VAT in the invoice currency is converted, or the net amount is converted first and the VAT rate applied to it. The Ministry of Finance describes the first method and uses it in its sample invoices; older tax rulings accepted the second. The results can differ by a grosz per VAT rate. With the gross method or a deposit invoice, the second method converts the gross amount and calculates the VAT from it. The VAT register in Dolibarr always holds what the invoice states. An invoice keeps the method it was issued with, and its corrections use the same one.
KSEF_FX_PLN_VAT_METHOD_convert_vat=Convert the VAT amount at the exchange rate (Ministry of Finance method, recommended)
KSEF_FX_PLN_VAT_METHOD_convert_base=Convert the net amount first, then calculate the VAT in PLN
KSEF_FX_KOR_METHOD=PLN VAT of a corrective invoice at the same rate
KSEF_FX_KOR_METHOD_Help=A corrective invoice uses the exchange rate of the invoice it corrects (VAT Act art. 31b ust. 1) and shows the change of the PLN VAT. The law accepts both ways of getting it (art. 106j ust. 2 pkt 5) and the Ministry of Finance names neither: the PLN VAT after the correction less the PLN VAT the corrected invoice showed, or the change in the invoice currency converted at the rate. They can differ by a grosz. When the corrected state has a different rate, only the first way gives a consistent result, so the module always uses it. Credit notes always convert their own amounts. The VAT register in Dolibarr follows what the corrections show either way. Corrections use the method of the first invoice in their chain.
KSEF_FX_KOR_METHOD_after_before=PLN VAT after the correction less PLN VAT shown before (recommended)
KSEF_FX_KOR_METHOD_change=Change in the invoice currency converted at the rate
KSEF_WoJsAccount=Pick an accounting account.
KSEF_WoJsSelect=Select an account
KSEF_WoErrAccountUnknown=%s: account %s is not in the active chart of accounts.
KSEF_PayRateText=rate %s (%s)
KSEF_PayFxInfoTitle=Value in zloty
KSEF_PayFxInfo=Dolibarr values this payment at the invoice rate: %s. At the NBP rate of the last working day before the payment date it would be %s (%s). Dolibarr does not book the difference of %s: the accountant does.
KSEF_PayFxInfoNoRate=Dolibarr values this payment at the invoice rate: %s. The NBP rate of the last working day before the payment date could not be fetched. The accountant books the exchange difference.
KSEF_CloseNoVat=Closing does not change VAT.
KSEF_CloseDiscountKor=A discount after the sale needs a corrective invoice:
KSEF_CloseKorLater="%s" becomes available on the invoice card once KSeF accepts the invoice.
KSEF_CloseDiscountRefused=A discount after the sale needs a corrective invoice, so this closing reason is not offered. Choose another reason or use "%s" on the invoice card.
KSEF_WoHelp=The remaining %s is written off to the selected account: debit this account, credit the customer, in the miscellaneous operations journal.
KSEF_WoHelpSupplier=The remaining %s is written off to the selected account: debit the supplier, credit this account, in the miscellaneous operations journal.
KSEF_WoJournalLabel=Write-off at closing
KSEF_WoReopenLedger=Invoice %s cannot be reopened: its write-off at closing is already in the ledger (%s). Delete that entry from the ledger first.
KSEF_DEPOSIT_FX_POLICY=Deposit in another currency used at another rate
KSEF_DEPOSIT_FX_POLICY_Help=When a deposit is deducted on the final invoice at another exchange rate, the same amount in the currency is a different amount in PLN. The VAT does not change: the deposit keeps its own rate and the final invoice converts only what is left (VAT Act art. 31a; tax rulings IPPP3-443-1046/10-2/JF and IPPP1/4512-1128/15-4/IGo). How the books show the net part is your accounting policy. At settlement: an exchange difference to financial income or costs when the deposit is settled (Accounting Act art. 30 ust. 4), the approach tax rulings take for income tax. Deposit's rate: the part the deposit covers stays revenue or cost at the deposit's rate (IAS 21 / IFRIC 22 through art. 10 ust. 3), for entities that follow IFRS. This only changes the explanations on invoice cards and in close notes; no amount, XML or accounting entry changes.
KSEF_DEPOSIT_FX_POLICY_settlement=Exchange difference at settlement (recommended)
KSEF_DEPOSIT_FX_POLICY_historical=Covered part kept at the deposit's rate (IFRS policy)
KSEF_FX_MULTI_RATE_ROUNDING=PLN VAT when one invoice uses several exchange rates
KSEF_FX_MULTI_RATE_ROUNDING_Help=An invoice for deliveries on different days converts each delivery at the NBP rate of its own day, and a deposit invoice for payments received on different days converts each payment at the rate of its day (VAT Act art. 19a and art. 31a). The law does not say whether the VAT in PLN is rounded once for each VAT rate or for each delivery or payment. The Ministry of Finance sample invoice converts each part and rounds once for each VAT rate; a 2023 tax ruling converts each delivery separately. The results can differ by a grosz. The VAT register in Dolibarr always holds what the invoice states. An invoice keeps the method it was issued with, and its corrections use the same one. Lines get their own rates only when the line supply dates are sent (Outgoing: Fields tab).
KSEF_FX_MULTI_RATE_ROUNDING_once=Convert each part, round once for each VAT rate (Ministry of Finance sample, recommended)
KSEF_FX_MULTI_RATE_ROUNDING_per_part=Round each delivery or payment separately
KSEF_ExtraFieldLineKurs=Exchange rate of the line (KSeF)
KSEF_LineRateMissing=This corrective invoice corrects an invoice whose lines were converted at different exchange rates (deliveries on different days). Its line "%s" did not come from the corrected invoice and has no date, so it is not known which delivery day's rate applies to it (VAT Act art. 31a and art. 31b ust. 1). Click Modify, enter on that line the date of the delivery it corrects and validate the invoice again: the module then uses the NBP rate of the last working day before that day. You can also create the corrective invoice from the corrected invoice's lines.
KSEF_LineRateNbpMissing=The lines of invoice %s were delivered on days with other NBP exchange rates, and each delivery is converted at the rate of its own day (VAT Act art. 31a ust. 1). Those rates could not be fetched from NBP, so the invoice cannot be sent yet. Try again in a while, or click Refresh next to the NBP rate on the invoice card once NBP is available.
KSEF_LineRatesNbpPending=Invoice %s: the NBP rates of its lines' delivery days could not be fetched now. It is validated with one rate; the line rates are set once NBP answers again, when you refresh the NBP rate or send the invoice. It is not sent without them.
KSEF_LineRatesFailed=Cannot set the exchange rates of the lines of invoice %s: %s
KSEF_LineRatesBooked=The lines of invoice %s were delivered on days with other NBP exchange rates, so each line must be converted at the rate of its own day (VAT Act art. 19a ust. 1 and art. 31a ust. 1). Its PLN amounts still use one rate, and Dolibarr no longer allows modifying the invoice (%s), so the module does not change them and the invoice is not sent. First undo that in Dolibarr (for example delete the payments or credits used on it, or its entries in the accounting ledger), then send the invoice (the line rates are set at the send) and record them again.
KSEF_LineRatesBookedKorDraft=The lines of invoice %s were delivered on days with other NBP exchange rates, so each line must be converted at the rate of its own day (VAT Act art. 19a ust. 1 and art. 31a ust. 1). Its PLN amounts still use one rate, and Dolibarr no longer allows modifying the invoice (%s), so the module does not change them and the invoice is not sent. Delete that draft corrective invoice and undo anything else listed, then send this invoice: the line rates are set at the send.
KSEF_LineRatesBookedKorIssued=The lines of invoice %s were delivered on days with other NBP exchange rates, so each line must be converted at the rate of its own day (VAT Act art. 19a ust. 1 and art. 31a ust. 1). Its PLN amounts still use one rate, and Dolibarr no longer allows modifying the invoice (%s), so the module does not change them and the invoice is not sent. That corrective invoice can only be sent to KSeF after this invoice: click Modify on its card and delete it, undo anything else listed, then send this invoice (the line rates are set at the send) and make the corrective invoice again.
KSEF_LineRatesSetAtSend=Invoice %s: its lines were delivered on days with other NBP exchange rates, so each line is now converted at the rate of its own day (VAT Act art. 31a ust. 1) and its PLN amounts were recalculated.
# Invoice rate set by the user in Dolibarr's own rate field; the lines' NBP rates
KSEF_ExtraFieldLineKursSrc=Source of the line's exchange rate (KSeF)
KSEF_TypedRateShort=set by the user
KSEF_TypedRateTableOf=table %s of %s
KSEF_TypedRateDiffers=The rate of this invoice, %s PLN for 1 %s, is not the NBP rate the module takes for its date: NBP's rate is %s (%s). The module treats it as a rate set by the user: it does not change it by itself and sends the invoice at this rate.
KSEF_TypedRateUseNbpHint=To use NBP's rate, enter %s in the "%s" field or click "%s".
KSEF_TypedRateUnverified=The rate of this invoice, %s PLN for 1 %s, is not the NBP rate the module took for it, and NBP's rate for its date could not be checked yet (NBP could not be reached). The module treats it as a rate set by the user: it does not change it by itself and checks it once NBP answers.
KSEF_LineRatesTitle=Exchange rates of the lines:
KSEF_LineRateOfInvoice=the invoice's rate
KSEF_LineRateNbp=NBP
KSEF_LineRateNbpForDay=NBP, for the delivery of %s
KSEF_LineRatesSettingOff=Invoice %s was validated while the setting "%s" (KSeF setup, Outgoing: Fields tab) was on, so each of its lines got the NBP rate of its own delivery day. The setting is now off, so the invoice would be sent with the sale date only and one rate, which changes its PLN amounts, and Dolibarr no longer allows modifying the invoice (%s). Set it back to "%s" and send the invoice again. To send it with the sale date only, first undo the items listed in Dolibarr, send the invoice, then record them again.
KSEF_LineRatesSettingOffNotice=Invoice %s: the setting "%s" is off, so the invoice is sent with the sale date only and its lines at the invoice's one rate; its PLN amounts were recalculated.
KSEF_DepositRatesSetAtSend=Invoice %s: its PLN amounts did not match the payments recorded on it, so each payment is now converted at the NBP rate of its own day (VAT Act art. 31a) and the PLN amounts were recalculated.
KSEF_DepositRateRestateRow=Payment rate
KSEF_DepositRateRestate=The payment of %s received on %s came before the invoice date, so its exchange rate is the NBP rate of the last working day before it, %s (VAT Act art. 31a ust. 1). The invoice sent to KSeF converts it at %s, so its PLN VAT is wrong. Issue a corrective invoice with the same amounts: it shows this payment at its own rate and the change of the PLN VAT.
KSEF_FX_DEPOSIT_KOR_ALLOC=Which payment a corrective invoice of a deposit invoice changes
KSEF_FX_DEPOSIT_KOR_ALLOC_Help=A deposit invoice for payments received on different days converts each payment at the NBP rate of its own day (VAT Act art. 19a ust. 8 and art. 31a). When its amount is corrected, the corrective invoice shows the change of each payment at that payment's rate (art. 31b ust. 1). The law does not say which payment a change concerns; that is agreed between you and the customer. Shared by amount spreads the change over all payments in proportion to their amounts. Newest payment first takes a lowering off the latest payment and adds a raise to it. The VAT register in Dolibarr always holds what the corrective invoice shows. A deposit invoice keeps the choice it was issued with, and all its corrective invoices use it.
KSEF_FX_DEPOSIT_KOR_ALLOC_proportional=Shared by the amounts of the payments (recommended)
KSEF_FX_DEPOSIT_KOR_ALLOC_newest_first=Newest payment first
KSEF_DepositPartsMax=Deposit invoice %s documents payments received on %s different days, but one invoice can state at most 31 such payments (the limit of the FA(3) structure), so it is not sent. Issue a separate deposit invoice in Dolibarr for the later payments: remove them from this invoice, lower its amount to the payments that stay on it, and record the later payments on the new deposit invoice.
KSEF_DepositCitesMax=The invoice refers to %s deposit invoices, but KSeF takes at most 100 of their numbers. The first 100 numbers will be sent.
KSEF_DepositPaymentOwnInvoiceRow=Payment without a deposit invoice
KSEF_DepositPaymentAfterSend=Of the payment received on %s, %s is more than the amount this deposit invoice states, and the invoice was already sent to KSeF. A sent invoice cannot be changed, and every payment received needs an invoice (VAT Act art. 106b ust. 1 pkt 4): issue a separate deposit invoice in Dolibarr for that amount. Delete this payment, record it again for the part this invoice states, and record the rest as a payment of the new deposit invoice. If that money came in the same month as the delivery or service it pays for, no deposit invoice is needed (art. 106b ust. 1a): the final invoice covers it, so record that part as a payment of the final invoice instead. The PLN amounts of this invoice were not recalculated.
KSEF_DepositPaymentAfterBooking=Of the payment received on %s, %s is more than the amount of this deposit invoice, and the invoice is already booked in accounting, so its amounts can no longer change. Every payment received needs an invoice (VAT Act art. 106b ust. 1 pkt 4): issue a separate deposit invoice in Dolibarr for that amount. Delete this payment, record it again for the part this invoice covers, and record the rest as a payment of the new deposit invoice. If that money came in the same month as the delivery or service it pays for, no deposit invoice is needed (art. 106b ust. 1a): the final invoice covers it, so record that part as a payment of the final invoice instead.
KSEF_DepositRefundNoCorrectionRow=Refund without a corrective invoice
KSEF_DepositRefundNoCorrection=Money was paid back to the customer (latest refund on %s), and %s of it is still in the amount this deposit invoice states: no corrective invoice lowers it. A returned deposit needs a corrective invoice (VAT Act art. 106j ust. 1 pkt 4): make the corrective invoice in Dolibarr, lowering this deposit invoice by that amount, and send it to KSeF.
KSEF_ForeignOwedRow=Left to pay in the invoice currency
KSEF_ForeignOwedOpen=In %s, %s is still left to pay, although the PLN amount is below zero (%s) because of the exchange rates. Enter the payment of the rest in the invoice currency, or close the invoice with the %s button and give the reason.
KSEF_ForeignOwedPartialNote=In %s, %s is still left to pay. The PLN amount is below zero (%s) only because of the exchange rates (for example a deposit or corrective invoice at a higher rate). Choose the reason for closing; the amounts in the reasons are in the invoice currency. The comment is optional.
KSEF_FA3_GROSS_SOURCE=Gross method (prices with VAT)
KSEF_FA3_GROSS_SOURCE_Help=Invoices issued with the gross method (art. 106e ust. 7-8): lines state the gross unit price and gross value instead of the net ones, and the VAT per rate is computed from the gross total. Corrections use the method of the invoice they correct. Cannot be used with the Dolibarr rounding mode MAIN_ROUNDOFTOTAL_NOT_TOTALOFROUND = 1. The tax per rate can differ by a few grosz from the VAT Dolibarr shows.
KSEF_SourceDisabled=Disabled
KSEF_SourceAlwaysOn=Always (every invoice)
KSEF_SourceInvoiceField=Invoice field
KSEF_SourceThirdpartyField=Third party field
KSEF_GrossMethodRoundingMode=The gross method (KSEF_FA3_GROSS_SOURCE) cannot be used with the rounding mode MAIN_ROUNDOFTOTAL_NOT_TOTALOFROUND = 1: Dolibarr then changes the gross total. Switch the rounding mode back or turn the gross method off.
KSEF_MarginMixedSubtypes=An invoice can use only one margin-scheme procedure (found: %s). Put the lines of each procedure on a separate invoice.
KSEF_SettlementReasonCreditNote=Settlement of corrective invoice %s
KSEF_SettlementReasonExcess=Settlement of overpayment %s
KSEF_FA3_UNIT_MAP_Title=Units of measure
KSEF_FA3_UNIT_MAP_Help=The text written as the unit of measure for each active Dolibarr unit when "Include Unit of Measure" is on. Leave empty to use the default: the module's Polish abbreviation, else the unit's short label.
KSEF_FA3_UNIT_Code=Unit
KSEF_FA3_UNIT_Text=Text in KSeF (empty = default)
KSEF_FA3_PAYMENT_FORM_MAP_Title=Payment forms
KSEF_FA3_PAYMENT_FORM_MAP_Help=The payment form written for each Dolibarr payment mode, on the invoice and on each partial payment. "Other" writes the form "other" with the name of the payment mode. An invoice without a payment mode gets no payment form. Payment modes the module does not know (e.g. BLIK added by you) default to "Other".
KSEF_PaymentFormDefault=Default: %s
KSEF_PaymentFormOther=Other (with the payment mode name)
KSEF_PaymentFormOmit=Do not write a payment form
KSEF_ExtraFieldPeriodFrom=Invoice period from (KSeF)
KSEF_ExtraFieldPeriodTo=Invoice period to (KSeF)
KSEF_ExtraFieldPeriodHelp=With both dates filled, the KSeF invoice states this period instead of the sale date.
KSEF_ExtraFieldOrderDate=Order date (KSeF)
KSEF_ExtraFieldOrderDateHelp=Written as the order date of the order number on the KSeF invoice.
KSEF_VAT_CODE_MARZA2=Margin scheme: travel services (art. 119)
KSEF_VAT_CODE_MARZA31=Margin scheme: second-hand goods (art. 120)
KSEF_VAT_CODE_MARZA32=Margin scheme: works of art (art. 120)
KSEF_VAT_CODE_MARZA33=Margin scheme: collectors' items and antiques (art. 120)
