# Pay supplier invoices from KSeF data
KSEF_PayFromKsef=Pay from KSeF data
KSEF_PayConfirmTitle=Payment from KSeF data
KSEF_PayConfirmQuestionValidate=Validate invoice %s and record the payment the seller reported in KSeF?
KSEF_PayConfirmQuestion=Record the payment of invoice %s that the seller reported in KSeF?
KSEF_PayKsefTotal=Invoice gross total
KSEF_PayCharge=Charge
KSEF_PayDeduction=Deduction
KSEF_PayKsefDue=Due according to the seller
KSEF_PayKsefDueHelp=The amount the seller states as due in KSeF: the invoice gross total plus charges (e.g. fees) minus deductions (e.g. a deposit). The difference to the invoice total is not owed: once this amount is paid the invoice is closed with the deductions in its closing note.
KSEF_PayAmount=Payment amount
KSEF_PayDueMismatch=The amount due stated by the seller (%s) does not equal the invoice gross total plus charges minus deductions (%s): check the amount; the invoice will not be classified paid automatically.
KSEF_PayDueMissing=The seller states no amount due; computed as the invoice gross total plus charges minus deductions: %s. The invoice will not be classified paid automatically.
KSEF_PayCloseInfo=Paying exactly %s classifies the invoice paid, with the KSeF deductions in the closing note. Any other amount leaves the rest open.
KSEF_PayChargesBeyondTotal=The amount due per KSeF (%s) is more than the remainder of this invoice (%s): the charges outside the invoice total must be paid separately.
KSEF_PayNothingToPay=KSeF: nothing to pay on this invoice (%s to settle or refund). Settle it manually.
KSEF_PayRefusedState=This invoice cannot be paid from KSeF data: it must be a draft, or validated with an amount left to pay, and the seller must have marked it paid.
KSEF_PayRefusedAmount=The payment amount must be more than zero and not more than the remainder to pay (%s).
KSEF_PayPaymentNote=Payment from KSeF data, invoice %s
KSEF_PayCloseNote=KSeF deductions: %s
KSEF_ForeignPaidCloseNote=Paid in full in %s. The PLN remainder (%s) is a rounding or exchange-rate difference, not an amount owed.
KSEF_CloseNoteRow=Closing note
KSEF_DepositCreditCovered=The deposit covered %s.
KSEF_DepositCreditCoveredMany=The deposits covered %s.
KSEF_DepositCreditLeftToPay=%s is left to pay.
KSEF_DepositCreditNothingLeft=In %s the invoice is paid in full.
KSEF_DepositCreditPlnBelowZero=The PLN amount is below zero because the deposit is converted at its own rate (%s) and the invoice at %s. It is not an overpayment, and the VAT in KSeF and JPK does not change.
KSEF_DepositCreditPlnBelowZeroMany=The PLN amount is below zero because the deposits are converted at their own rates (%s) and the invoice at %s. It is not an overpayment, and the VAT in KSeF and JPK does not change.
KSEF_DepositFxSplit_settlement=At the invoices' rates, %s of it is the net part: in the books usually a %s exchange difference that arises when the deposit is settled (Accounting Act art. 30 ust. 4).
KSEF_DepositFxSplit_historical=At the invoices' rates, %s of it is the net part: under your policy of keeping the deposit's rate (IAS 21 / IFRIC 22) it stays %s at the deposit's rate, not an exchange difference.
KSEF_DepositFxVatPart=The other %s is the deposit's VAT, which stays at the deposit's rate: a difference between the VAT Dolibarr records here and the deposit's own VAT, not an exchange difference.
KSEF_DepositFxPositive=positive
KSEF_DepositFxNegative=negative
KSEF_DepositFxRevenue=revenue
KSEF_DepositFxCost=cost
KSEF_ForeignPaidCloseNoteFx_settlement=Paid in full in %s. The PLN left (%s) is due to the deposit's rate (partly an exchange difference) and is not owed.
KSEF_ForeignPaidCloseNoteFx_historical=Paid in full in %s. The PLN remainder (%s) comes from the deposit's own rate, not an amount owed.
KSEF_DepositCreditPlnRow=Foreign-currency deposit
KSEF_DepositCreditPlnRemainLabel=below zero because of the deposit's rate, not an overpayment
KSEF_DepositCreditPlnNoExcess=This amount cannot be turned into an available credit: in %s the invoice is not overpaid.
KSEF_ClassifyPaidCurrencyOwed=The invoice is not paid: in %s, %s is still left to pay. The PLN amount comes from the exchange rates and does not mean it is paid. Enter the payment of the rest in the invoice currency.
KSEF_ClassifyPaidCurrencyOwedRest=Through REST it can be closed only with a reason: give close_code (for example other) and, if you like, close_note with a description.
KSEF_ClassifyPaidCurrencyOwedDeposit=If the rest of the deposit will not be paid, use "Corrective invoice" on the deposit invoice's card to lower it to the amount actually received.
KSEF_ClassifyPaidCurrencyOwedDepositSupplier=If the rest of the deposit will not be paid, ask the supplier for a corrective invoice lowering the deposit invoice to the amount actually paid, and enter it in Dolibarr (one sent through KSeF is imported on the Incoming Invoices page).
KSEF_CreditNoteCreditCovered=The corrective invoice covered %s.
KSEF_CreditNoteCreditCoveredMany=The corrective invoices covered %s.
KSEF_CreditsMixedCovered=The deposits and corrective invoices covered %s.
KSEF_CreditNoteCreditPlnBelowZero=The PLN amount is below zero because the corrective invoice is converted at its own rate (%s) and this invoice at %s. It is not an overpayment, and the VAT in KSeF and JPK does not change.
KSEF_CreditNoteCreditPlnBelowZeroMany=The PLN amount is below zero because the corrective invoices are converted at their own rates (%s) and this invoice at %s. It is not an overpayment, and the VAT in KSeF and JPK does not change.
KSEF_CreditsMixedPlnBelowZero=The PLN amount is below zero because the deposits and corrective invoices are converted at their own rates (%s) and this invoice at %s. It is not an overpayment, and the VAT in KSeF and JPK does not change.
KSEF_CreditNoteFxSplit=At the invoices' rates, %s of it comes from the corrective invoices: in the books usually a %s exchange difference that arises at the set-off (Accounting Act art. 30 ust. 4); for income tax usually only the net part, %s, counts.
KSEF_DepositFxSplitMixed_settlement=On the deposits, the difference at the invoices' rates is %s, of which %s is the net part: in the books usually a %s exchange difference that arises when the deposit is settled (Accounting Act art. 30 ust. 4).
KSEF_DepositFxSplitMixed_historical=On the deposits, the difference at the invoices' rates is %s, of which %s is the net part: under your policy of keeping the deposit's rate (IAS 21 / IFRIC 22) it stays %s at the deposit's rate, not an exchange difference.
KSEF_DepositFxVatPartMixed=The other %s of it is the deposits' VAT, which stays at their rate: a difference between the VAT Dolibarr records here and the deposits' own VAT, not an exchange difference.
