KSEF_CorrectionReportSupplierRow=Original supplier invoices deducted:
KSEF_CorrectionReportSupplierVatRow=VAT of the original supplier invoices deducted from the VAT to get back
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsTitle=Corrections in reports
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_Reports=Corrections in reports
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsIntro=A correction (corrective invoice) keeps the original invoice booked and counts only for its difference, in the month of the correction. Dolibarr reports that let modules change them are adjusted by the module; the others count the original and the full correction. Supplier corrections (imported upward KSeF corrections) are adjusted the same way in the purchases journal, the VAT reports and income and expenses, but not in the supplier balance (supplier card) or the turnover statistics. With deposits as payments (FACTURE_DEPOSITS_ARE_JUST_PAYMENTS), a deposit's corrections and credit notes count 0 in the journals and reports, like the deposit itself (not on the VAT-on-payment lines).
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsColReport=Report
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsColEffect=How corrections appear
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsJournal=Accountancy: sales journal and ledger
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsJournalEffect=Adjusted: the correction is booked as its difference per account (customer, income, VAT). With a customer deposit account (ACCOUNTING_ACCOUNT_CUSTOMER_DEPOSIT), bind a deposit's corrections (corrective invoices of a deposit, credit notes on such a correction) to that account on the binding page: Dolibarr suggests it only for the deposit and credit notes made directly on it.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsRecap=Customer accounting summary (customer card, Accounting tab)
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsRecapEffect=Adjusted: the correction is listed as its difference.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsVat=VAT reports: summary, by rate, by customer
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsVatEffect=Adjusted with explicit rows "Correction: original invoice ... deducted" (negative amounts per line of the original), also for a rate the correction removed and when the original is in an earlier period. Sales whose VAT is due on payment (cash method) are not adjusted: the page shows a notice. Only payments received above a corrected value (excess credit) are taken back, with a row "Payments above the corrected value of invoice ... taken back" in the month of the correction; when that credit later pays another invoice, it counts again as a payment of that invoice in the month of the set-off (row "Excess credit from the correction of invoice ... used as payment"). The set-off date is the day the credit was applied; change it on the paying invoice's card (Set-off date of the used credit), for example to the date of a set-off agreement. Credit applied before version 1.5.0 has no recorded date: the date of the paying invoice's latest payment is used, else its close date, else its invoice date. A credit refunded outside Dolibarr stays taken back.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsResult=Income and expenses (mode invoices / bills), summary and detail
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsResultEffect=Adjusted: the summary per month; in the detail a separate section "KSeF corrections" deducts the originals per customer and their VAT, Profit is corrected, Income and Outcome are corrected in the browser (the customer rows above keep Dolibarr's figures).
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsLocaltax=Local taxes (not used in Poland)
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsLocaltaxEffect=Not adjusted.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsStats=Turnover statistics (Billing and payment, Reports: turnover, by customer, by user), invoice statistics and graphs, customer card totals, REST totals of outstanding invoices
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsStatsEffect=Not adjusted (Dolibarr does not let modules change them): the original and the full correction both count. Use the VAT reports or the accountancy journal for corrected figures.
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsSimple=Accounting (simplified) module: sales journal
KSEF_HowTo_Corrections_ReportsSimpleEffect=Not adjusted (Dolibarr does not let modules change it). With deposits as invoice lines Dolibarr leaves corrections out of this journal entirely; with deposits as payments it lists the original and the full correction.

