KSEF_PhoneTooLongLeftOut=Phone number of %s is longer than 16 characters even without spaces and dashes: it is left out of the KSeF invoice (contact data). Shorten it in the third party card to send it.
KSEF_GvFlagNoMember=The customer %s has "%s" ticked on its card, so the invoice says it concerns a VAT group member, but it names no member (third entity with role 10). KSeF accepts it as it is. Add the member as a third entity with role 10, or untick the box on the customer card if the invoice does not concern a member.
KSEF_JstFlagNoUnit=The customer %s has "%s" ticked on its card, so the invoice says it concerns a subordinate local government unit, but it names no unit (third entity with role 8). KSeF accepts it as it is. Add the unit as a third entity with role 8, or untick the box on the customer card if the invoice does not concern a unit.
KSEF_GvJstPodmiot3Off=The invoice names a VAT group member or a JST unit as a third entity (role 10 / 8), but third entities are turned off in the outgoing invoice settings: it is not sent, so the invoice will not say it concerns a group member or unit.
KSEF_ForeignPlnVatMismatch=The VAT in PLN that Dolibarr records for this invoice differs from the VAT in PLN that the invoice states, converted from the invoice currency at the NBP rate (%s). The VAT register and JPK would not match what KSeF receives, so the invoice is not sent. Fetch the NBP rate on the invoice again, or align the amounts with the Database check on the About tab of the module setup.
KSEF_ForeignPlnVatMismatchLegacy=This invoice was validated by a module version before 1.5.0: the VAT in PLN that Dolibarr records differs from the VAT in PLN that the invoice states, converted from the invoice currency at the NBP rate (%s). KSeF receives the converted VAT, as the VAT act requires, so the VAT register differs from it by these amounts. While the invoice is unsent, unpaid and not booked, the Database check on the About tab of the module setup can align the amounts in Dolibarr.
KSEF_ForeignPlnVatBeforeMismatch=The corrected invoice %s was sent to KSeF with a VAT in PLN other than the one Dolibarr records for it (%s). This corrective invoice states the change from the VAT sent to KSeF, so the change in Dolibarr's VAT register differs from it by the same amount.
KSEF_ForeignPlnVatItem=%s: Dolibarr %s, invoice %s
KSEF_VatRateNotPolish=VAT rate %s%% is not a Polish rate and KSeF will not accept it. Support for foreign rates is planned in a future version of the module. Correct the line VAT rate.
KSEF_SaleDateInKsef=Sale date in KSeF
KSEF_SaleDateReplacedByPeriod=Replaced by the invoice period %s - %s: the KSeF invoice carries no single sale date.
KSEF_SaleDateReplacedByLineDates=Replaced by a date on every line: the KSeF invoice carries no single sale date.

# REST API: sync
KSEF_HowTo_RestSync=Incoming sync: <b>POST /incoming/sync</b> starts a round (a KSeF export), <b>POST /incoming/sync/advance</b> moves it on (call it again while the answer is PROCESSING, DOWNLOADING or PROCESSING_BATCHES; COMPLETED with more = true: start the next round), <b>GET /incoming/sync/status</b> only reads the state. <b>POST /incoming/sync/reset</b> without parameters clears a stuck fetch; with <b>from_date</b> (YYYY-MM-DD) or <b>days_back</b> it moves the sync point back, which only an administrator may do.
KSEF_HowTo_RestApplyLine=Credit note applied as lines (<b>apply-line</b>): in KSeF the credit is declared as a settlement of the target invoice (settlement block, deduction entry), not as a price reduction: the target's lines, VAT and totals stay as sold and the amount due is reduced. The alternative is <b>apply-payment</b> (the credit used as a payment of a validated invoice).

