KSEF_NoteAccountCurrency=The bank account on the invoice (%s) is in %s, the invoice in %s
KSEF_NoteAccountCurrencyHow=This account number goes to KSeF as the account to pay to. The account is right if the customer pays in %s. If they pay in %s, choose in the "%s" field the account %s.
KSEF_MainCurrencyNotPln=Dolibarr's main currency is %s, not PLN
KSEF_MainCurrencyNotPlnFix=KSeF invoices state their amounts in złoty, and Dolibarr issues invoices in the main currency. Set "%s" to PLN in Setup > Company/Organization before you issue invoices. A draft saved earlier in another currency can then be switched to PLN on its card.
KSEF_MainCurrencyOpen=Open the company setup
KSEF_CurrencyNoMulticurrency=The invoice is in %s while the Multicurrency module is off, so no NBP rate can be fetched. See the note above the invoice card.
KSEF_NoteCurrencyStray=The invoice is in %s while the main currency is %s
KSEF_NoteCurrencyStrayFix=The draft was saved while the main currency was different. The Multicurrency module is off, so no NBP rate can be fetched for this currency and the invoice cannot be sent. "Fix" switches the draft to %s. The amounts stay as they are, so check the prices.
KSEF_NoteCurrencyStrayValidated=The Multicurrency module is off, so no NBP rate can be fetched for this currency and the invoice cannot be sent. Set the invoice back to draft with "Modify" and use "Fix" in this note, or enable the Multicurrency module and fetch the NBP rate.
KSEF_NoteCurrencyStrayConfirm=Switch the draft to %s
KSEF_NoteLineVat=A line's VAT is not net × VAT rate
KSEF_NoteLineVatWhy=Dolibarr computes a line's VAT as gross minus net, each rounded, so with a unit price below one cent the VAT is a cent off. A line's VAT is net × rate, rounded to the cent. "Fix" sets that VAT (gross = net + VAT) and updates the invoice totals. The net does not change. Without the fix the invoice is sent with Dolibarr's amounts.
KSEF_NoteLineVatBooked=The invoice is already in accounting, so the module will not change it. Delete its accounting entries and come back here, or send it with Dolibarr's amounts.
KSEF_NoteLineVatConfirm=Set the line VAT to net × rate
KSEF_NoteRowLineVat=VAT of line %s (%s)
KSEF_NoteRowLineGross=Gross of line %s (%s)
KSEF_LineVatLine=line %s "%s"
KSEF_LineVatItem=%s: net %s, VAT in Dolibarr %s, while %s of the net is %s
KSEF_LineVatSendWarning=A line's VAT is not net × VAT rate: %s. Without the fix the invoice is sent with Dolibarr's amounts.
KSEF_LineVatFixLink=Fix the line VAT
KSEF_NoteDepositStale=The credit from deposit %s is %s; after the correction it should be %s.
KSEF_NoteDepositFix="Fix" changes only the unused credit and the draft invoices that deduct it. Payments and invoices sent to KSeF stay as they are.
KSEF_NoteDepositConfirm=Fix the deposit credit
KSEF_NoteDepositHeld=This cannot be fixed now: validated invoice %s deducts the old amount. Set it back to draft with the "Modify" button, then come back here.
KSEF_NoteDepositSent=Settlement invoice %s, sent to KSeF or booked, deducts the old amount of deposit %s.
KSEF_NoteDepositSentFix=The module will not change that invoice. Issue its correction with the button on its card: the correction starts from the deposit's current amount.
KSEF_NoteDepositSentFixHere=The module will not change this invoice. Issue its correction with the "Settlement corrective invoice" button on this card: the correction starts from the deposit's current amount.
KSEF_NoteDepositSentSupplier=The module does not change it. Ask the supplier for a correction of the settlement invoice.
KSEF_NoteRowDepositCredit=Credit from deposit %s
KSEF_NoteRowDeduction=Deduction on invoice %s
