KSEF_NoteForeignPln=PLN amounts do not match the conversion at %s PLN per 1 %s: %s.
KSEF_NoteForeignPlnFix="Fix" converts the PLN amounts again from the %s amounts (those stay). The VAT register will match the invoice sent to KSeF.
KSEF_NoteForeignPlnFixRound="Fix" converts the PLN amounts again from the %s amounts. The VAT in that currency changes by the rounding of the total.
KSEF_NoteForeignPlnConfirm=Convert PLN amounts again
KSEF_NoteForeignPlnLocked=The module will not change this invoice because Dolibarr no longer allows modifying it: %s. Correct the %s difference in accounting.
KSEF_NoteForeignPlnSent=The invoice is already in KSeF, so the module does not change it. Correct the %s difference in accounting.
KSEF_NoteImportRate=Imported at %s PLN per 1 %s, but the KSeF invoice states %s PLN per 1 %s. All PLN amounts are wrong.
KSEF_NoteImportRateFix="Fix" sets the KSeF rate and converts the PLN amounts again. The %s amounts stay.
KSEF_NoteImportRateAlso=It also changes the corrections: %s.
KSEF_NoteImportRateConfirm=Set the KSeF rate
KSEF_NoteImportTotalsConfirm=Set the totals to KSeF's
KSEF_NoteImportRateLocked=The invoice is paid, settled, booked or has a credit note, so the module will not change it. Correct the PLN amounts in accounting (VAT %s instead of %s).
KSEF_NoteRowRate=Rate (PLN per 1 %s)
KSEF_NotePaidOwed=The invoice is marked paid, but the %s payments are %s short.
KSEF_NotePaidOwedBefore=Closed before the module was updated to 1.5.0.
KSEF_NotePaidOwedHow=Dolibarr closes an invoice when payments and credits cover the PLN amount, and does not check the %s amount. That is why it shows "%s".
KSEF_NotePaidOwedWhat=What to do depends on what happened:
KSEF_NotePaidOwedClose=Less arrived because a bank or operator deducted a fee or converted at its own rate: if the invoice is to stay closed without this amount, nothing needs doing. To record the shortfall with a reason, use "%s", then "%s" with the reason "%s" (when the bank converted at its own rate: "%s").
KSEF_NotePaidOwedCloseSupplier=The supplier accepted less because its bank deducted a fee or the bank converted at its own rate: if the invoice is to stay closed without this amount, nothing needs doing. To record the shortfall with a reason, use "%s", then "%s" with the reason "%s".
KSEF_NotePaidOwedCloseAccount=With the Accounting module on, the window also asks for the account the PLN shortfall is booked to.
KSEF_NotePayColumn=Payment %s was entered in %s, but the account "%s" is in %s.
KSEF_NotePayColumnWhy=Dolibarr converted it at the invoice rate and recorded %s in the bank. Compare that with the %s statement:
KSEF_NotePayColumnOk=The amount matches the statement: reconcile this bank entry ("%s") and the note goes away.
KSEF_NotePayColumnRedo=It does not match: delete the payment on its card (button below) and enter it again, with the statement amount in the %s column.
KSEF_NotePayColumnRedoClosed=It does not match: use "%s", delete the payment on its card (button below) and enter it again, with the statement amount in the %s column.
KSEF_NoteIndexPayColumn=Payment in another currency than its account
KSEF_PayColumnHint=This account is in %s: enter the amount in the "%s" column so it matches the statement.
KSEF_PayAccountOtherCurrency=This account is in %s and the invoice in %s: choose an account in the invoice currency. Dolibarr would record the invoice amount in the bank as an amount in the account currency.
KSEF_NotePaidOwedPayReopen=The customer will pay the rest: use "%s", then enter the missing amount in %s with the "%s" button.
KSEF_NotePaidOwedPayReopenSupplier=You will pay the supplier the rest: use "%s", then enter the missing amount in %s with the "%s" button.
KSEF_NotePaidOwedKeep=The customer paid in full or will not pay the rest: leave the invoice closed. The %s shortfall comes from the exchange rates (for example a deposit at another rate), and in PLN the invoice is settled.
KSEF_NotePaidOwedKeepSupplier=You paid the supplier in full or will not pay the rest: leave the invoice closed. The %s shortfall comes from the exchange rates (for example a deposit at another rate), and in PLN the invoice is settled.
KSEF_NotePaidOwedWrongReopen=A payment was entered with the wrong amount: use "%s", delete the payment with the "%s" button on the payment card and enter it again.
KSEF_NoteExcessOwed=Dolibarr turned an "overpayment" of %s into a credit, but the %s payments are %s short.
KSEF_NoteExcessOwedWhy=Dolibarr turns a PLN amount above the invoice into a credit and does not check the %s amount. That is why it shows "%s". A payment can only be added to an open invoice, and the credit has to be deleted first:
KSEF_NoteExcessOwedDo=Delete this credit in the third party's discounts (button below).
KSEF_NoteExcessOwedUsed=The credit is already deducted on %s: unlink it there, then delete it in the third party's discounts.
KSEF_NoteExcessOwedReopen=Reopen the invoice with the "%s" button.
KSEF_NoteExcessOwedPay=The customer will pay the rest: enter the missing amount in %s with the "%s" button. The customer paid in full and the difference comes from a bank fee or the exchange rate: close the invoice with the "%s" button and a reason.
KSEF_NoteExcessOwedPaySupplier=You will pay the supplier the rest: enter the missing amount in %s with the "%s" button. The supplier accepted less and the difference comes from its bank's fee or the exchange rate: close the invoice with the "%s" button and a reason.
