# NBP rate date method (art. 31a ust. 2a-2c)
# ============================================
KSEF_NBP_RATE_DATE_METHOD=NBP rate date
KSEF_NBP_RATE_DATE_METHOD_Help=Which day decides the NBP table used for foreign currency invoices. VAT rules (default): the table before the earlier of the invoice date and the sale date; for an intra-EU supply the invoice date, but no later than the 15th of the month after the delivery; a deposit invoice uses the day it was paid. Income tax rules (VAT Act art. 31a ust. 2a): the table before the day the revenue arises, that is the sale date, or the invoice date or the full payment date when earlier; also for intra-EU supplies. Deposit invoices keep the VAT rule, because under income tax a deposit is not revenue yet. Corrections always keep the rate of the invoice they correct. Choose the rule your accounting policy uses: the income tax rule binds for at least 12 months, and after giving it up the VAT rules apply for at least 12 months.
KSEF_NBP_RATE_DATE_METHOD_VAT=VAT rules (tax point)
KSEF_NBP_RATE_DATE_METHOD_INCOME_TAX=Income tax rules (day revenue arises)
KSEF_NBP_RATE_DATE_METHOD_Since=Rule chosen on %s
KSEF_NBP_RATE_DATE_METHOD_EarlyLeave=The income tax rule was chosen on %s. The VAT Act (art. 31a ust. 2b) binds that choice for at least 12 months, until %s. The setting was saved, but until that date the law does not allow going back to the VAT rules.
KSEF_NBP_RATE_DATE_METHOD_EarlyReturn=The income tax rule was given up on %s. After giving it up, the VAT rules apply for at least 12 months (VAT Act art. 31a ust. 2c), until %s. The setting was saved, but until that date the law does not allow going back to the income tax rule.

