KSEF_Tour_ConfirmSend=Check the preview and the environment, then click "Send to KSeF" in this window: only then does the invoice go to KSeF. "Cancel" closes the window without sending; the validated invoice stays unsent in Dolibarr and you send it later with "Send to KSeF" on the card.
KSEF_Tour_Sent=Invoice accepted in KSeF (status "Accepted"): its KSeF number is in this window. "Save to PC" and "Print" give the PDF with the QR code. Click "Close"; the guide shows the status on the invoice card.
KSEF_Tour_KorDate=The invoice date is empty and it is required: type it or click "Now" (today). Then click "OK".
KSEF_Tour_StatusNotAccepted=The invoice is not accepted in KSeF yet. The "KSeF send status" row, when the card shows it, says what happened: after an error it gives the reason, with a button to send again. Without that row the invoice was not sent: go back with the "<" arrow to the sending step.
KSEF_Tour_DepositAck=The module warns before sending: the window says which deposit of the order is not deducted and why (e.g. not paid). To settle it, click "Cancel": the guide goes back to the invoice card. If this is intended (e.g. a partial delivery), tick the box in the window and click the framed "Send anyway" button.
KSEF_Tour_Backdated=The invoice date is earlier than today. The window says what that means for sending: "Send online" sends the invoice with its own date, "Set date to today" (drafts only) changes the invoice date to today. "Cancel" leaves the invoice unsent. Click the button you choose in the window.
KSEF_Tour_SendFailed=Sending failed: the window gives the reason and what to do next. "Try Again" sends the invoice once more; "Close" leaves it unsent. When KSeF is down, issue the invoice offline: see the guide "Offline invoice: KSeF outage or backdated".
KSEF_Tour_None_Accepted=The list has no standard invoice accepted in KSeF in the current environment, so this guide has nothing to correct. Send an invoice first, e.g. with the guide below. An invoice issued outside KSeF is corrected from its card with "Corrective invoice".
KSEF_Tour_None_AcceptedDeposit=The list has no deposit or settlement (final) invoice accepted in KSeF in the current environment. You correct only an invoice that is in KSeF already: issue and send a deposit first, e.g. with the guide below.
KSEF_Tour_None_Replace=This customer has no invoice that can be corrected here (the list entries are greyed). Click the "Back" arrow in this box and choose another customer, start from the card of the invoice to correct (button below), or send an invoice to this customer first.
KSEF_Tour_None_Deposit=The list has no deposit accepted in KSeF in the current environment and not deducted yet. A settlement (final) invoice deducts earlier deposits, so issue and send a deposit first. When there was no deposit, issue a standard VAT invoice. Both guides are below.
KSEF_Tour_None_Credit=This customer has no deposit to deduct now. The deposit must be accepted in KSeF, paid and available as credit (the first steps of this guide). If no deposit was issued yet, issue one with the guide below.
KSEF_Tour_None_Order=The list has no validated customer order that is not billed yet. Issue the invoice without an order ("Without an order" button below), or create and validate an order first, then start this guide again.
KSEF_Tour_None_Offline=The list has no invoice to issue offline: no sending failed and there is no unsent invoice dated before today. Such an invoice appears when KSeF does not answer at sending, or when you validate a draft with an earlier date later. To practise, click "New backdated invoice": the guide takes you through it.
KSEF_Tour_None_OfflineCard=This invoice can now be neither sent again nor issued offline: the status next to it gives the reason (e.g. KSeF rejected it or found it a duplicate). Go back with the "<" arrow to the list and pick another invoice, or issue a new one with the guide below.
KSEF_Tour_None_Incoming=The list has no purchase invoice to import (status New). Fetch the invoices from KSeF first: click "Sync Now" above the list (it also fetches sales invoices), or start the guide below.
KSEF_Tour_None_IncomingKor=The list has no corrective invoice to import (status New). Fetch the invoices from KSeF first: click "Sync Now" above the list (it also fetches sales invoices), or start the guide below. If it is still missing after fetching, the supplier has not issued a correction.
KSEF_Tour_None_IncomingDeposit=The list has no deposit or settlement (final) invoice to import (status New). Fetch the invoices from KSeF first: click "Sync Now" above the list (it also fetches sales invoices), or start the guide below.
KSEF_Tour_None_Fetched=The list is empty: no purchase invoice has been fetched yet. Click "Sync Now" above the list and wait for the page to reload. If the list stays empty, KSeF has no invoices issued to your NIP.
KSEF_Tour_None_Sales=There are no KSeF invoices missing in Dolibarr: nothing to import. Skipped invoices (the badge with the crossed-out eye) are not counted here; click that badge to see them. When you issue an invoice in another program, click "Sync Now" (here or on the KSeF dashboard) and start this guide again.
KSEF_Tour_ImportConfirm=The "Are you sure you want to import this invoice?" window: check the supplier and the lines, then click "Import". "Will be created" next to the supplier means the import adds it to the third parties. "Cancel" returns to the import page.
