KSEF_Tour_setup_company_langsave=Click "Save": the identifier fields get their Polish names and the names message goes away.
KSEF_Tour_setup_env=KSeF environment
KSEF_Tour_setup_env_Desc=Test, Demo or Production.
KSEF_Tour_setup_env_select=Choose the environment. Start with Test: fictitious data, no legal effect. Demo: your real data, invoices without legal effect. Production: real invoices; a warning shows under the field and, after saving, a confirmation window.
KSEF_Tour_setup_env_save=Click "Save". Without saving, the module stays in the previous environment.
KSEF_Tour_setup_env_confirm=The module asks in a window whether to switch it to PRODUCTION. Check the NIP in the window and click "Yes": from now on you send real invoices. "No" keeps the previous environment.
KSEF_Tour_setup_env_boxes=Each environment has its own login data. The active one has a green frame. You enter the token or certificate in the next guide.
KSEF_Tour_setup_env_boxes_saved=Each environment has its own login data. The active one has a green frame. Its login data is saved already: in the next guide you check that the login works.
KSEF_Tour_setup_env_portal=You generate the token and certificate in the KSeF Taxpayer Application of this environment (link below, new tab). Log in with an electronic signature (qualified or Trusted Profile). Generate a token with the rights to issue and view invoices, or a KSeF certificate.
KSEF_Tour_setup_env_portal_test=You generate the token and certificate in the KSeF Taxpayer Application of this environment (link below, new tab). Log in with an electronic signature (qualified or Trusted Profile); Test also accepts a self-signed certificate and is for made-up data (a random NIP). Generate a token with the rights to issue and view invoices, or a KSeF certificate.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth=Token or certificate
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_Desc=Logging in to KSeF and testing the connection.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_token=Paste into the framed field the token from the KSeF Taxpayer Application for the %s environment (link below) and click "OK".
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_token_replace=A token for the %s environment is saved already (it is not shown). It works: leave the field empty and click "OK". To replace it, paste a new token from the KSeF Taxpayer Application (link below) and click "OK".
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_offline_ok=Logging in to KSeF works in this environment: the test result is stored. The offline certificate (optional) is needed only for invoices in offline mode (QR code II). It is a separate KSeF certificate of the offline type: you generate it in the KSeF Taxpayer Application of this environment (link below). You have the files: in the framed form choose "Certificate File" (.crt), "Private Key File" (.key), type the "Private Key Password" when the key has one, and click "Save Offline Certificate". You do not issue offline invoices: click "Next guide".
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_savetoken=Click "Save" under the token: it saves the token and switches the login to the token. Without saving, the pasted token is lost.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_cert=You generate a KSeF certificate of the authentication type in the KSeF Taxpayer Application of this environment (link below); you get a certificate file and a private key. In the framed form choose "Certificate File" (.crt), "Private Key File" (.key), type the "Private Key Password" when the key has one, and click "Save Authentication Certificate". No files yet: click "Next", the guide tells you what is missing.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_switch=The certificate is saved, but the login still uses the token. To log in with the certificate: select "Certificate Authentication" and click "Next". Staying with the token: click "Next" without changes.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_savemethod=Click "Save" under the token: only then does login switch to the certificate.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_testauth=Check the login: click "Test Token Authentication". A green message at the top of the page means the login works; the module stores the result and ticks the checklist item. Red: the guide goes back to the token field and says what to fix.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_testauth_failed=The login test failed: the red message at the top of the page gives the reason. Most often the token was generated for another NIP than the company NIP in the KSeF settings, or the token expired. Paste the right token from the KSeF Taxpayer Application into the framed field and click "OK"; after saving, the guide asks for the test again. When the token is valid but was generated for another NIP, fix the company NIP in the KSeF settings (guide "Company NIP and address").
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_testcert=Check the login: click "Test Certificate Authentication". A green message at the top of the page means the login works; the module stores the result and ticks the checklist item. Red: the guide goes back to the certificate form and says what to fix.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_way=How should the module log in to KSeF in the %s environment? A token is the simplest. A KSeF certificate (a .crt file with a .key) is the other way.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_way_token=With a token
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_way_cert=With a KSeF certificate
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_cert_failed=Saving the certificate or the certificate login test failed: the red message at the top of the page gives the reason (most often the key does not match the certificate, the password is wrong, the certificate was issued for another NIP or environment, or it expired). Choose the right files again and click "Save Authentication Certificate"; then the guide asks for the test.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_offline=The offline certificate (optional) is needed only for invoices in offline mode (QR code II). It is a separate KSeF certificate of the offline type: you generate it in the KSeF Taxpayer Application of this environment (link below). You have the files: in the framed form choose "Certificate File" (.crt), "Private Key File" (.key), type the "Private Key Password" when the key has one, and click "Save Offline Certificate". You do not issue offline invoices: click "Next guide".
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_offline_saved=The offline certificate is saved (green frame in the form): offline invoices get QR code II. You upload a renewed certificate with the same form.
KSEF_Tour_setup_auth_offline_failed=The offline certificate was not saved: the red message at the top of the page gives the reason (most often a missing file, a key that does not match the certificate, or a wrong password). Choose both files again, type the password and click "Save Offline Certificate".
KSEF_Tour_None_AuthTest=There is no login test button here: it shows once a token and the company NIP in the KSeF settings are saved. Save the token ("<" arrow) or fill in the NIP with the guide below.
KSEF_Tour_None_AuthCert=No authentication certificate is saved, so there is nothing to test. You need two files from the KSeF Taxpayer Application of this environment: the certificate (.crt) and the private key (.key), plus the key password when it has one. Once you have them, run this guide again or log in with a token.
KSEF_Tour_Stage_offline=Offline certificate
KSEF_Tour_Gate_setup=Before you start: this setting is missing, and without it the module cannot log in to KSeF. Complete it (link next to it). The guide checks it by itself each time you come back to the page and starts once nothing is missing.
KSEF_Tour_setup_vat=VAT codes
KSEF_Tour_setup_vat_Desc=Zero-rate codes: exempt, np I, np II, 0 WDT, 0 EX, reverse charge, margin scheme.
KSEF_Tour_setup_vat_table=Tick the codes you use: ZW (exempt), NP (np I, outside the country), NP2 (np II, services to EU businesses), WDT (intra-EU supply), EX (export), RC (reverse charge), MARZA2, MARZA31, MARZA32, MARZA33 (margin scheme). Ticked codes appear in the VAT rate list of invoice lines. You use only the 23, 8 and 5%% rates: tick nothing.
KSEF_Tour_setup_vat_save=Save the ticked codes with "Save".
KSEF_Tour_setup_vat_none=You use only the 23, 8 and 5%% rates? Click "Not applicable": the checklist item is closed.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults=Invoice defaults
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_Desc=Payment terms and method, bank account, sale date, notes.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_term=Default Payment Terms: the payment due date of new invoices for a customer without terms of their own. Goes to KSeF as the payment due date. The field is optional; with no default terms leave it empty.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_saledate=Default Date of Sale Source: "Linked delivery/order date" puts the shipping date, the order delivery date or the order date on the invoice when they exist. "Invoice date" puts nothing: the sale date is then the invoice date.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_method=Default Payment Method: for invoices without a chosen method (e.g. Bank transfer). Without it the invoice goes to KSeF without a payment form.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_bankon=The default bank account goes on invoices paid by transfer (the account number in KSeF), but the Banks and Cash module is off. Click "Enable" next to the bank account: the module is switched on and you come back here. You give no account on invoices: click the "Next" arrow in this box.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_bankadd=There is no bank account yet. Click "Add an account": the chosen payment term and method are saved first, then Dolibarr's account form opens; after you save it, the new account becomes the default account of invoices and you come back here.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_bankform=The company's new bank account: type a short "Ref." (e.g. BANK1) and the "Bank or cash label", check the account type, the currency (PLN) and the country, type the account number (IBAN) in the account part, and at the bottom of the form click the button that creates the account. After saving, the module makes it the default and returns to the settings.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_bank=Default Bank Account: put on transfer invoices that have no account of their own.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_notes=Public Note Mode: whether the invoice note goes to KSeF as a footer, as an additional description, or as Key:Value pairs.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_save=Save with "Save" at the bottom of the form.
KSEF_Tour_setup_defaults_savefields=This tab has its own "Save" button at the bottom.
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming=Automatic fetching and scheduled jobs
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming_Desc=The purchase invoice fetching job and the other module jobs.
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming_cron=State of the "Download incoming invoices" job. While it is off, you fetch invoices by hand only. You switch it on from its card, which this guide leads to.
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming_sync="Sync Now" fetches new purchase and sales invoices at once, without waiting for the job. The same button is on the Outgoing invoices page and on the KSeF dashboard.
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming_jobs=The module's scheduled jobs and their state. The required jobs ("Download incoming invoices", "Download UPO confirmations", "Check the status of sent invoices") are on. "Offline deadlines" and "KSeF availability (Latarnia)" warn about offline deadlines and KSeF outages. A job that is on but has not run yet waits for its first run by the server's job scheduler.
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming_enablejobs=Some required jobs are off (the row names them). Click "Enable the required jobs": the module switches them all on at once.
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional=Optional: NBP, chart of accounts, GUS, permissions
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_Desc=Rates job, chart of accounts for write-offs, company lookup by NIP, permissions.
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_noacc=Optional: NBP, GUS, permissions
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_noacc_Desc=Rates job, company lookup by NIP, permissions.
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_nbp=NBP rates: every foreign-currency invoice gets its NBP rate at sending anyway. The rates job (optional) updates the Multi currency rates daily, so the PLN amounts on screen are current. Click Next.
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_gus=GUS: when on, the module fills in the name and address of a Polish third party from its NIP. In the test environment GUS works without a key; for production enter the key from GUS (a sample key request is in How to use). Optional.
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_rights=Permissions: click the login of the user who should get KSeF rights. The guide shows their "Permissions" tab.
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_rights_admin=Permissions: there is only the administrator, who has all rights. You give KSeF rights to new users here: click the user's login, then the "Permissions" tab.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat=Standard VAT invoice
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_Desc=From a new invoice to the UPO; foreign currency and 0 percent codes on the way.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_customer=Choose the customer (type a few letters of the name or the NIP). The page reloads after the choice. Add a new customer with the plus button next to the field: the guide leads you through its form. When you start from the customer card, it is filled in already.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_saledate=Sale date (delivery or service date): enter it when it differs from the issue date. Left empty, the module takes it by the "Default Date of Sale Source" setting.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_save=Click "Create draft". The guide continues on the invoice card.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_nbp=Foreign currency invoice: the NBP rate and table date used for KSeF. When the rate is missing or out of date (marked yellow), fetch it with the button next to it.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_send=Click "Validate and send to KSeF" (or "Send to KSeF" for a validated invoice). The click validates the draft at once (the invoice gets its number). The module first shows its confirmation window, unless "Confirmation before uploading to KSeF" is off in the settings.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_status=KSeF send status: once accepted it shows the KSeF number and date, and the links "Download XML FA(3)" and "Download UPO" download the sent file and the official receipt. Clicking the KSeF number opens the Ministry of Finance KSeF verification page of this invoice in a new browser tab.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_tab=The KSeF tab holds every send attempt, error and the UPO of this invoice. Click it; the guide shows it in the last step.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_tabpage=The send history of this invoice: date, environment, the "%s" column (e.g. "Accepted"), the KSeF number and the "%s" column with its description, if any. The icons in the "%s" column download the UPO and the send files. The "Customer invoice" tab takes you back to the invoice card.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor=Corrective invoice
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_Desc=Correcting an invoice already in KSeF.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_way=A corrective invoice can start from the invoice you correct ("Corrective invoice" button on its card) or from a new invoice (type "Corrective invoice", then pick the invoice). Choose one; both end in the same corrective invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_way_card=From the invoice to correct
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_way_new=From a new invoice
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_customer=New invoice: choose the customer of the invoice to correct. Dolibarr lists that customer's invoices once one is chosen (the page reloads).
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_newform=Pick the invoice to correct in this list. "Corrective invoice (any change)" is then chosen as the type.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_pick=The list shows standard invoices accepted in KSeF in the current environment. Click the number of the invoice to correct. The guide continues on its card. Deposit and settlement invoices are corrected with the guide "Corrective invoice of a deposit or settlement (final) invoice".
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_button="Corrective invoice" makes a corrective invoice for any change: amounts, rates, lines, buyer data. The credit note next to it is an alternative only for lowering amounts or a return of goods; this guide leads through the correction. Click "Corrective invoice".
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_creditnote=A credit note is the alternative when you only lower amounts or take goods back. The guide goes through the corrective invoice: click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_form=The form already has the correction of this invoice chosen.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_creditform=The form already has the credit note of this invoice chosen. Enter the amounts or lines to take back.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_save=The correction of the invoice is already selected on the form. Click "Create draft". The guide continues on the correction card.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_details=Correction reason (optional): choose it from the list and KSeF gets it. You give no reason: click "OK".
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_detailsave=You may leave "Correction type" empty; choose it only when the correction should take effect from the original invoice's date or another date. Then click "Save" in this row.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_lines=The lines were copied from the corrected invoice. Change a line with the framed pencil or delete it with the bin, so the invoice looks as it should after the correction; add a new line in the row below the list ("Add"). The module works out the differences; a correction without changes corrects nothing. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_KorLinesEditing=Change the values in the row being edited.
KSEF_Tour_KorLinesEditingFx=Invoice in a foreign currency: change the price in the field with the currency symbol, e.g. "U.P. (net) (€)", and leave the PLN price as it is. After "Save" the module recomputes the PLN price and amounts at the invoice's NBP rate.
KSEF_Tour_CustomerChosen=The customer is already chosen (framed row). Click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_send=Click "Validate and send to KSeF". The module first shows its confirmation window, unless "Confirmation before uploading to KSeF" is off in the settings.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_status=Once accepted, the correction has its own KSeF number; the corrected invoice is marked Corrected. Clicking the KSeF number opens the Ministry of Finance KSeF verification page of the correction in a new browser tab.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal=Deposit invoice
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_Desc=A deposit from an order or without one; you settle it with the settlement (final) invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_way=A deposit is best issued from the customer order: KSeF then gets the order value, and you enter the deposit as an amount or a percentage. Without an order you create an empty deposit invoice and add a line with the deposit amount.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_way_order=From an order (recommended)
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_way_new=Without an order
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_order=Click the number of the customer order you take the deposit for. The list shows validated orders not invoiced yet. When the order already has a deposit, Dolibarr says so on the invoice form: this is another deposit for that order. The customer has no order: click "<" and choose "Without an order".
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_createbill=Click "Create Invoice". When the create buttons are gathered under one "Create" button, open it first.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_customer=New invoice: choose the customer first (type a few letters of the name or the NIP). The page reloads after the choice.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_type=Choose the type "Deposit invoice".
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_amount=Type the gross deposit amount: "%s" is already selected in the list next to it. Instead of an amount you can choose "%s" (percentage of the order value in one line) or "%s" (percentage of each order line). With a fixed amount the module splits the deposit across the order's VAT rates.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_save=Click "Create draft". The guide continues on the invoice card.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_summary=The "KSeF invoice type" row: a deposit invoice "without an order". KSeF gets no order value, only the deposit amount from the line.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_summary_order=The "KSeF invoice type" row: deposit invoice, the order and its value (in brackets), as they go to KSeF. Earlier deposits for this order are deducted together with this one on the settlement invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_send=Click "Validate and send to KSeF". The module first shows its confirmation window, unless "Confirmation before uploading to KSeF" is off in the settings.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_status=The deposit is accepted in KSeF: the status row shows its KSeF number and the files to download. When the customer pays, record the payment (guide "Pay a deposit"); after delivery you settle it with the final invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz=Settlement (final) invoice
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_Desc=The settlement (final) invoice deducts earlier deposits; paying the deposit on the way.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_deposit=The deposit first: the list shows deposits accepted in KSeF in the current environment that no other invoice has deducted yet. Under each deposit number are its order and payment state. Click the number of the deposit you settle. When the order has several deposits, click any of them: the final invoice deducts all of them. Preferably an unpaid one, since the guide helps you pay it right away.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_pay=This deposit is not paid yet, and only a paid deposit can be deducted on the settlement invoice. When the customer has paid, click "Enter payment": the guide "Pay a deposit" takes you through the payment and comes back here. Record only a payment the customer has already made.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_convert=The deposit is paid but not a credit yet. Click "Mark as credit available": only then can the deposit be deducted on the settlement invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_convertyes=Confirm in the Dolibarr window with "Yes".
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_ready=This deposit is accepted in KSeF, paid and ready to be deducted on the settlement invoice. Click Next to create that invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_send_cert=Click "Validate and send to KSeF" ("Send to KSeF" for a validated invoice, "Retry sending" after a failed attempt). The click validates the draft. For a backdated invoice the module offers to issue it offline; when KSeF does not answer, the failure window opens.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_offconfirm_core=Confirm issuing offline with "Yes" in the Dolibarr window. "No" leaves the invoice validated but not sent. If KSeF does not accept it at once, the deadline for sending shows on the invoice card.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_way_order_none=From an order (no order to invoice)
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_way_order_none=From an order (no order to invoice)
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_confirm=The "Are you sure you want to import this invoice?" window: check the supplier, the correction's lines and which original invoice the correction replaces, then click "Import". "Cancel" returns to the import page.
KSEF_Tour_recv_import_supplier_missing=Seller: the module did not find the supplier by NIP. Choose it from the list, or keep "Automatically create suppliers when no match is found" ticked and the import creates a new supplier. When "Fetch supplier data from GUS" is ticked too (and GUS lookup is on), the new supplier's name and address come from the REGON register, not from the invoice; untick it to keep the invoice data.
KSEF_Tour_None_IncomingAfter=The sync is done, but the list still has no invoice to import: KSeF has no new invoice for your NIP. You need not sync again; the guide ends here.
KSEF_Tour_update_apply_done_fix=Done: the update is applied. The database check below lists items to repair; they may have existed before the update. Each has a description and a repair button.
KSEF_Tour_Stage_details=Correction details
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_send_open=Click "Validate and send to KSeF". Not all the order's deposits are deducted, so the module warns first; in that window you confirm the sending or go back to the invoice.
KSEF_Tour_SendConfirmNote=The module first shows its confirmation window.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_pay_manual=Click "Enter payment": the guide leads you through the payment form. On a settlement invoice you pay the amount after the deposits.
KSEF_Tour_recv_fetch_cron_off=The "Download incoming invoices" job is off, so you fetch invoices only with "Sync now". Switch on automatic fetching with the guide "Automatic fetching and scheduled jobs".
KSEF_Tour_GateNoFix=You cannot change these settings with your account: ask the Dolibarr administrator.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_amount_pct=Type the percentage of the order value the deposit covers. The module works out the gross amount from the order and splits it across its VAT rates; for a fixed amount change the choice in the list next to it.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_form_saledate=Type "Sale date" (delivery or service date) when it differs from the issue date; left empty, it is taken by the "Default Date of Sale Source" setting.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_customer_chosen=The deposit's customer is already chosen (framed row): the settlement invoice must have the same customer as the deposit. Click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_way=The settlement invoice is best made from the same order: the lines come from the order. Without an order you create a normal invoice and add the lines of the whole order.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_way_order=From an order (recommended)
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_way_new=Without an order
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_order=Click the number of the order whose deposits you settle (the order number is on the deposit card, under "Related Objects"). The list shows validated orders not billed yet. An invoice without an order: click "<" and choose "Without an order".
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_createbill=Click "Create Invoice". When the create buttons are gathered under one "Create" button, open it first.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_customer=New invoice: choose the customer whose deposits you settle (type a few letters of the name or the NIP). The page reloads after the choice.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_save=Click "Create draft". The guide continues on the invoice card.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_deposits=In the "Discounts or credits available" row choose the deposit and click "Apply" (once per VAT rate); on an invoice from an order the "Apply the deposit" button at the start of that row applies all its deposits at once. The module recognises the settlement invoice by the applied deposits. The deposit is missing from the list when it was not marked as credit available (the first steps of this guide), is not paid, or was already deducted on another invoice. Without an applied deposit this invoice goes to KSeF as a plain VAT invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_deposits_done=Deposits applied: the "KSeF invoice type" row shows a final invoice without warnings, and each deducted deposit is a line with a negative amount, one per VAT rate. Click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_credit=Invoice without an order: in the "Discounts or credits available" row choose the credit of the deposit you settle (the deposit number is in the credit's description). A deposit with several VAT rates has a separate credit per rate: apply each of them.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_creditapply=Click "Apply": the deposit's credit becomes an invoice line with a negative amount, and the module recognises the settlement invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_summary=The "KSeF invoice type" row: a settlement invoice and the deducted deposits, as they go to KSeF. Hover a deposit number to see its KSeF number. The invoice amounts already take the deducted deposits into account.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_send=Click "Validate and send to KSeF".
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_send_nodeposit=Note: no deposit is deducted on this invoice, so it goes to KSeF as a plain VAT invoice, not as a settlement invoice. To settle a deposit, click "<" and apply it in the "Discounts or credits available" row. If that is intended, click "Validate and send to KSeF".
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_status=The final invoice is accepted in KSeF. The "KSeF invoice type" row lists the deducted deposits; their KSeF numbers are in the invoice's XML file (link "Download XML FA(3)"). When you correct a deposit later, the card shows a warning and the "Settlement corrective invoice" button.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_status_nodeposit=Invoice accepted in KSeF as a plain VAT invoice: no deposit was deducted on it. To settle a deposit, issue a new settlement invoice with this guide and apply the deposit on it.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal=Corrective invoice of a deposit or settlement (final) invoice
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_Desc=The module picks the correction type itself.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_way=Start from the deposit or settlement invoice you correct ("Corrective invoice" button on its card) or from a new invoice (type "Corrective invoice", then pick the invoice). Choose one; both end in the same corrective invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_way_card=From the invoice to correct
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_way_new=From a new invoice
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_customer=New invoice: choose the customer of the invoice to correct. Dolibarr lists that customer's invoices once one is chosen (the page reloads).
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_newform=Pick the deposit or settlement invoice to correct in this list. "Corrective invoice (any change)" is then chosen as the type.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_pick=The list shows deposit and settlement (final) invoices accepted in KSeF in the current environment. Click the number of the invoice to correct. The guide continues on its card.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_creditnote=A credit note is the alternative when you only lower a deposit or a settlement invoice. The guide goes through the corrective invoice: click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_settle=A settlement invoice already sent whose deposit was corrected afterwards shows this warning (the deposit card names it too). "Settlement corrective invoice" makes its corrective invoice with the deposit at its new value.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_button="Corrective invoice" is the recommended way for any change to a deposit or settlement invoice, up or down; the module picks the kind of correction from how the original was sent. The credit note next to it serves only to lower; this guide leads through the correction. Click "Corrective invoice".
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_form=The form already has the correction of this invoice chosen.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_creditform=The form already has the credit note of this invoice chosen. Enter the amount to take back.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_save=The correction of the invoice is already selected on the form. Click "Create draft". The guide continues on the correction card.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_details=Correction reason (optional): choose it from the list (e.g. Change of the deposit amount) and KSeF gets it. You give no reason: click "OK".
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_detailsave=You may leave "Correction type" empty; choose it only when the correction should take effect from the original invoice's date or another date. Then click "Save" in this row.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_lines=Click the pencil in the line you change (the pencils of all lines are framed) and type the new amount. The module works out the difference. Do not apply the credit of the corrected deposit on this correction.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_lines_editing=Type the new amount in the "U.P. (net)" field of the edited line: the deposit value after the correction, not the difference.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_lines_editing_fx=Invoice in a foreign currency: type the new amount in the field with the currency symbol, e.g. "U.P. (net) (€)": the deposit value after the correction, not the difference. Leave the PLN price as it is; after "Save" the module recomputes it at the invoice's NBP rate.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_lines_roz=The lines were copied from the settlement invoice. Change them with the pencil, delete them with the bin or add new ones in the row below. The deducted deposit row stays as it is: the module deducts the deposit at its current value. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_send=Click "Validate and send to KSeF". The module first shows its confirmation window, unless "Confirmation before uploading to KSeF" is switched off in the settings.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_status=The correction is sent; the "KSeF invoice type" row shows "Corrective invoice of a deposit invoice" or "Corrective invoice of a settlement invoice".
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_status_settle=The correction's KSeF status; the "KSeF invoice type" row shows "Corrective invoice of a deposit invoice". The warning in that row names the settlement invoice that deducts the deposit as it was before: it needs a correction too. Open it from the link and click "Settlement corrective invoice".
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_status_overpaid=KSeF status of the correction; the "KSeF invoice type" row shows a deposit correction. The correction lowered a deposit already paid: the message in that row gives the overpayment. Refund it to the customer or keep it as a deposit for a next invoice, as the message says.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_status_zal=The deposit correction is sent; the "KSeF invoice type" row shows "Corrective invoice of a deposit invoice". When the correction raised the deposit, the missing amount shows on this correction as remaining to pay; record its payment with "Enter payment" when the customer pays. When it lowered a deposit already paid, refund the overpayment or keep it for the next invoice; the deposit card gives the amount.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_status_roz=The correction of the settlement invoice is sent; the "KSeF invoice type" row shows "Corrective invoice of a settlement invoice".
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_tab=The KSeF tab of this correction shows the corrected invoice and its KSeF number. Click the tab; the guide shows its content in the last step.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_tabpage=The corrected invoice and the KSeF number the correction cites; below, the send history of the correction. The "Customer invoice" tab takes you back to the correction card.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline=Offline invoice: KSeF outage or backdated
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_Desc=Issuing offline during a KSeF outage or for a backdated invoice, the sending deadline; needs an offline certificate.
KSEF_Tour_GuideNeedsOfflineCert=no offline certificate
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_latarnia=This guide covers two cases: a KSeF outage and a backdated invoice (issued earlier outside KSeF). The framed box is the KSeF system status (Latarnia): outages and maintenance announced by the Ministry of Finance. When KSeF is down, Latarnia shows it here; you then issue invoices offline.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_pick=The list shows invoices to issue offline: with a failed sending in the current environment, or unsent and dated before today (no credit notes). Click the invoice number.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_send=Click "Validate and send to KSeF" ("Send to KSeF" for a validated invoice, "Retry sending" after a failed attempt). The click validates the draft. When KSeF does not answer, the failure window opens. For a backdated invoice without an offline certificate the "Backdated invoice" window opens: there you choose "Send online" or, on a draft, "Set date to today".
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_failure=Error window: KSeF did not answer. "Try Again" sends the invoice once more. "Issue Offline Invoice" issues it at once with QR codes (needs an offline certificate; without it an administrator sees "Set up Offline certificate"). "Close" leaves the invoice unsent; you send it later.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_backdated=Backdated invoice, no offline certificate: "Send online" sends it with its own date, "Set date to today" (drafts only) changes the invoice date to today and sends. "Cancel" leaves the invoice unsent. Issuing offline needs an offline certificate.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_offline=Issue offline: the invoice gets its QR codes now and must reach KSeF by the deadline; the module uploads it when KSeF works again.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_offconfirm=Confirm issuing offline: click "Issue offline". "Cancel" leaves the invoice validated but not sent. If KSeF does not accept it at once, the deadline for sending shows on the invoice card.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_deadline=The deadline for sending the offline invoice to KSeF. After it the module warns, but the invoice can still be sent.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_status=The KSeF sending status of this invoice: once accepted, the KSeF number and date. An invoice issued offline that KSeF has not accepted yet waits here to be sent.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales=Own invoices from KSeF: fetch, match, rebuild
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_Desc=Invoices in KSeF where you are the seller, also sent from other software.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_sync=Click "Sync Now": it fetches from KSeF the invoices where you are the seller, and the purchase invoices as well. It only reads, it sends nothing. Wait until the page reloads. The same button is on the KSeF dashboard.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_counts=Match with KSeF: each badge is the number of invoices in one state; hover it to see what it means. Only the badges of states that hold invoices are shown. Clicking a badge shows only those invoices in the list.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_filter=Click the framed number: the list shows only the invoices Dolibarr lacks.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_missing=This invoice is in KSeF but not in Dolibarr. Click the framed import icon: it rebuilds it from the KSeF XML.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_adjust=The arrows icon in the Actions column opens the adjustment of an invoice that differs from KSeF in Dolibarr. Click it.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_import=The import page: customer, lines and products read from the KSeF XML. Check them before importing.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_importbtn="Import" creates the invoice in Dolibarr, already linked to its KSeF number. Nothing is sent to KSeF.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_confirm=The "Are you sure you want to import this invoice?" window: check the buyer and the lines, then click "Import". "Will create" next to the buyer means the import adds it to third parties. Nothing is sent to KSeF.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_compare=The comparison: fields that differ from KSeF are marked. "Match to KSeF" saves the KSeF version.
KSEF_Tour_send_sales_done=Done: the invoice is in Dolibarr. The "KSeF Submission Status" row shows its KSeF number and the "In KSeF since" date: when the invoice reached KSeF, not a send from Dolibarr. Nothing was sent to KSeF.
KSEF_Tour_recv_fetch=Fetching purchase invoices
KSEF_Tour_recv_fetch_Desc=Sync, the incoming list and its statuses.
KSEF_Tour_recv_fetch_sync="Sync now" fetches purchase invoices issued to your NIP, and also your own sales invoices stored in KSeF. The same button is on the KSeF dashboard.
KSEF_Tour_recv_fetch_cron=The "Download incoming invoices" job does the same automatically when it is on: it fetches purchase and sales invoices (guide "Automatic fetching and scheduled jobs").
KSEF_Tour_recv_fetch_list=Incoming invoices: each row is one invoice from KSeF. Column "Status": New (to import), Imported, Skipped, Error.
KSEF_Tour_recv_fetch_open=Open an invoice to see its card.
KSEF_Tour_recv_fetch_card=Invoice card: the data from the XML. "Import to Dolibarr" makes a supplier invoice from it (guide "Importing a purchase invoice"). "Download FA(3) XML" gets the file from KSeF, "Download PDF" its visualisation, and "Verify on KSeF portal" opens the Ministry of Finance KSeF verification page of the invoice.
KSEF_Tour_RecvPickCard=This is the card of an invoice fetched from KSeF. Click the framed "Import to Dolibarr" button: it opens the import page.
KSEF_Tour_recv_import=Importing a purchase invoice
KSEF_Tour_recv_import_Desc=Supplier match or create, product mapping.
KSEF_Tour_recv_import_pick=Click the number of an invoice with the status New, e.g. in the framed row, and on its card "Import to Dolibarr"; or straight away the import icon in the Actions column.
KSEF_Tour_recv_import_supplier=Seller: the module found the supplier by NIP. "Change" lets you choose another.
KSEF_Tour_recv_import_supplier_msg=Seller: the module looks the supplier up by NIP. Found: "Change" lets you pick another one. Not found: choose it from the list, or leave "Auto-create suppliers when no match found" ticked and the import creates a new supplier from the invoice data. "Fetch Supplier Data from GUS" then fills in its name and address from the REGON register (when the GUS lookup is on). After the import icon on the list, the message at the top of the page says the same; close it with its cross.
KSEF_Tour_recv_import_lines=Lines: link each one to a Dolibarr product in the "Product (optional)" column, or leave the field empty and the line stays a text line (the invoice's description).
KSEF_Tour_recv_import_import=Click "Import". A summary window opens first; the supplier invoice is created in Dolibarr only after you confirm.
KSEF_Tour_recv_import_done=Supplier invoice created by the import and validated, linked to its KSeF number. Record its payment with "Enter payment" on this card.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor=Incoming corrective invoice
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_Desc=Linking to the original; refused while the original is missing.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_pick=Click the number of a correction (KOR in the Type column) with status New, e.g. in the framed row, and on its card "Import to Dolibarr".
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_corrects=The original invoice this correction corrects, given by its KSeF number (with a link when it is on the incoming invoice list).
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_missing=The original invoice is not among the invoices fetched from KSeF yet. Click "Fetch it from KSeF": its import page opens; after its import the guide comes back to this correction.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_missing_import=The original invoice is fetched from KSeF already but is not in Dolibarr. Click "Import the original invoice first": its import page opens; after its import the guide comes back to this correction.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_missing_never=The correction does not give the KSeF number of the original invoice, so it cannot be fetched. Create the original invoice in Dolibarr by hand, then come back to the import of this correction.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_origimport=Click "Import" and confirm in the window. After the import you are back on the import page of the correction.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_origconfirm=The "Are you sure you want to import this invoice?" window: check the supplier and the lines of the original invoice, then click "Import". The guide continues on the import page of the correction.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_info=The correction replaces the original invoice: it has the amounts after the correction, the original invoice gets the status Corrected, and what remains to pay is the amount on the correction (the original's payments stay on it and reduce that amount).
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_refused=The original invoice is not in Dolibarr: the import is refused. Import the original first; when it is not in KSeF, create it in Dolibarr by hand.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_strategy=How the correction is booked against the original.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_import=Click "Import" once the original invoice is in Dolibarr; you confirm the import in a window.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_done=The correction is imported as a supplier invoice with the amounts after the correction. The original invoice has the status Corrected, and what remains to pay is the amount on this correction (less the original's payments).
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits=Incoming deposit and settlement invoices
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_Desc=Deposits become supplier credits; the settlement (final) invoice deducts them.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_pick=The deposit first, then the settlement: import and pay the deposit invoice (ZAL), only then the final invoice (ROZ), so that it deducts the deposit. Click the number of an invoice with the status New, e.g. in the framed row, and on its card "Import to Dolibarr".
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_deposits=Settled deposits: each deposit the settlement invoice cites. The import deducts only deposits that are imported and paid; the others show why not.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_lines=Invoice lines: link each one to a Dolibarr product in the "Product (optional)" column, or leave it empty (a text line). On a settlement invoice the deposit deduction is a separate line with a negative amount; the module adds it by itself on import.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_import=Click "Import": a deposit invoice goes to Dolibarr as a supplier deposit invoice, a settlement invoice deducts the imported and paid deposits. You confirm the import in a window.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_pay=When KSeF marks the invoice as paid, "Pay from KSeF data" records the payment for the amount left after the deposits. Otherwise click "Enter payment": the guide leads you through the payment form.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_pay_zal=Pay the deposit: "Pay from KSeF data" when KSeF marks it as paid, or "Enter payment": the guide leads you through the payment form. The settlement invoice deducts only a paid deposit.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_payask=The "Payment as per KSeF data" window: the payment fields, and above them the amount to pay as per the seller (after the deposits, if any). Check them and click "Yes": the payment is recorded. "No" closes the window without a payment.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_done=The settlement invoice is in Dolibarr, linked to its KSeF number; the imported and paid deposits are deducted from it.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_done_zal=The deposit is in Dolibarr, linked to its KSeF number. Once it is paid, import the settlement invoice: the "Import the next deposit or settlement" button starts this guide from its first step.
KSEF_TourPick_All=Show all invoices
KSEF_TourPick_Note_offline=List filtered by the guide: invoices that can be sent again or issued offline.
KSEF_TourPick_Note_roz=List filtered by the guide: deposits accepted in KSeF in the current environment, not deducted on another invoice yet.
KSEF_TourPick_Note_korzal=List filtered by the guide: deposit and settlement invoices accepted in KSeF in the current environment.
KSEF_TourPick_Note_kor=List filtered by the guide: plain invoices accepted in KSeF in the current environment.
KSEF_TourPick_Order=order %s
KSEF_TourPick_Settlement=settlement
KSEF_TourPick_Deposit=deposit
KSEF_Tour_recv_import_again=Import the next invoice
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_again=Import the next deposit or settlement
KSEF_Tour_CustomerNew=New customer: enter the name and address, and the NIP in the "%s" field, then click "Create third party" at the bottom of the page. Dolibarr returns to the new invoice with this customer and the guide continues.
KSEF_Tour_None_OtherEnv=This invoice is not accepted in KSeF in the current environment (the "KSeF Submission Status" row names another environment), so you cannot correct it here. Click "<" to go back to the list, or send an invoice in this environment first, e.g. with the guide below.
KSEF_Tour_OffConfirm=The invoice date is before today, so the module offers to issue it offline: the invoice gets its QR codes at once and goes to KSeF with this date; the invoice card shows the sending deadline. Click "Issue offline". "Cancel" leaves the invoice unsent; you send it later from the card.
KSEF_Tour_CronCardOn=The job is on ("Enable scheduling" is gone). To run by itself, the server cron must run the Dolibarr script scripts/cron/cron_run_jobs.php every few minutes.
KSEF_Tour_LinkCron=Turn on the Scheduled jobs module
KSEF_Tour_LinkCronHelp=How to set up the job scheduler (How to use)
KSEF_Tour_LinkCompany=Complete the company details (Setup > Company/Organization)
KSEF_Tour_SideCompany=The company data in the form above: first choose the country (Poland; the page reloads), then type the company name, the address, the zip and the town, and set the main currency to the zloty (type Zloty in the search field). Then click the framed "Save" button, and at the end "Go back" in this box: the guide returns to the KSeF settings.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_price_fx=Foreign-currency invoice: type the net unit price in the invoice currency, in the column marked with its symbol (e.g. €), not in the PLN column. For a listed product Dolibarr fills in only the PLN price; fill in the invoice-currency field yourself.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_price_fx_noprod=Foreign-currency invoice: type the net unit price in the invoice currency, in the column marked with its symbol (e.g. €), not in the PLN column.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_fxprod=Foreign-currency invoice, the line first: in the framed cell pick a product or service from the list or type a description (a line not from the list: choose the type too, Product or Service), then click Next. You type the price in the invoice currency in the next step: picking a product enters its price in zloty and clears the currency field.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_fxprod_noprod=Foreign-currency invoice, the line first: in the framed cell type a description and choose the type, Product or Service, then click Next. You type the price in the invoice currency in the next step.
KSEF_Tour_AddrowFx=A line in a foreign currency: the product or description and the price in the invoice currency are filled in. Check the VAT rate and the quantity, then click "Add".
KSEF_Tour_AddrowFxEmpty=The price in the invoice currency is empty (picking a product or a change in the row cleared it). Type it again in the column marked with the currency symbol (e.g. €), check the VAT rate and the quantity, and only then click "Add".
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_nbp_fetch=The foreign-currency invoice has no NBP rate yet. Click the framed "{label}" button: the module fetches the rate from the NBP table by the rule in the KSeF settings and shows the table date.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_nbp_ok=Foreign currency invoice: the NBP rate is already fetched. Check the NBP table date in this row; the module converts the VAT to zloty at this rate, and the rate and the VAT in PLN go to KSeF. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_nbp_account=Foreign currency invoice: check the NBP table date in the rate row. The note on the card says the invoice's bank account is in another currency than the invoice: a PLN account is right when the buyer pays in zloty; otherwise choose the account in the invoice currency, as the note says. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_pay_partial=This deposit is paid only partly (payments on the card), and only a fully paid deposit can be deducted on the settlement invoice. The customer pays the rest: click "Enter payment" and enter the missing amount when you receive it. The customer paid less and will not pay more: instead of a payment, issue a correction of the deposit to the amount paid (guide "Corrective invoice of a deposit or settlement (final) invoice").
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_origin=This deposit comes from the order shown under "Related Objects", so you create the settlement invoice from the same order. Click its number.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_deposits_apply=Click the framed "{label}" button: the module deducts all deposits of this invoice's order from it (accepted in KSeF, paid and marked as available credit), each in its VAT rates. The list in the "Discounts or credits available" row also holds credits from this customer's other orders; when you pick from it by hand, pick the credit of this order's deposit (its number is in the credit description).
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_deposits_warn=The "KSeF invoice type" row says what is missing (e.g. a deposit not paid yet or another one to apply). When a deposit waits for payment, the next step points at its payment button, leads through the payment and comes back here. When this is intended (e.g. a partial delivery), click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_deposits_unpaid=The "KSeF invoice type" row says a deposit of this order still waits for its payment. Click Next: the next step points at its payment button, leads through the payment and comes back here.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_payother=Click the framed "{label}" button: the guide leads through the payment of this deposit and then comes back to this invoice, to the deposits step. The deposit is to stay unpaid (e.g. a partial delivery): click ">", and the invoice deducts only the paid deposits.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_status_online=The invoice was accepted in KSeF online (sent at once, or sending again worked), so no offline deadline applies.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_status_offaccepted=Invoice issued offline and already accepted in KSeF: the status shows the offline issue date and the date it was sent to KSeF. The offline deadline was met.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_status_failed=Sending failed: the status gives the reason. When KSeF was not reachable, use "Retry" or issue the invoice offline. When KSeF rejected it, fix the invoice as the error says (details on the KSeF tab); offline does not help.
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming_cronoff=The Scheduled jobs module is off, so no KSeF module job runs: you fetch invoices by hand only, with "Sync Now". Turn that module on (link below), then click "Go back" on the module list: the guide goes on.
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming_card=Click "Job card" next to the "Download incoming invoices" job: it opens its card in Dolibarr.
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming_croncard=The card of the "Download incoming invoices" job. Click "Enable scheduling". You switch the other module jobs on the same way from their cards (About tab). To run by themselves, the server cron must run the Dolibarr script scripts/cron/cron_run_jobs.php every few minutes; without it you run a job by hand only.
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_nbpopen=To switch the rates job on, click "Job card": it opens its card. Without this job click ">".
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_nbpcard=The card of the "NBP rates for Multicurrency currencies" job. Click "Enable scheduling", then Next.
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_permtab=Click the "Permissions" tab.
KSEF_Tour_setup_optional_perms=The KSeF module in the permissions list. "Read KSeF submissions and incoming invoices" lets the user view these; "Send to KSeF and manage KSeF records" lets them send invoices and import purchase invoices. Grant a right with the button next to it; expand the module when its rights are hidden. Sending also needs the right to create and edit customer invoices.
KSEF_Tour_recv_fetch_dash=The "Sync with KSeF" block: when purchase and sales invoices were last fetched and how many. Sales invoices missing in Dolibarr are shown by the link in the outgoing row (guide "Own invoices from KSeF: fetch, match, rebuild"). Click Next.
KSEF_Tour_None_FetchedAfter=After the sync the list is still empty: KSeF has no purchase invoices issued to your NIP in this environment. No need to sync again; the job or "Sync Now" fetches new invoices once a supplier issues them.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_pick_sync=There are corrections on the list, but the invoices they correct are not among the ones fetched from KSeF yet. First click the framed "Sync now" button: it fetches the missing invoices. When they are still missing after the sync, the guide points at the correction and the import shows what is missing.
KSEF_Tour_recv_kor_missing_failed=The original invoice could not be fetched: KSeF does not have it (message at the top of the page). You cannot import this correction until the original invoice is in Dolibarr: create it by hand as a supplier invoice, then come back to the import of this correction. The guide ends here.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_supconfirm=Check the amount, keep "Yes" and click "Validate". Dolibarr records the payment and returns to the supplier invoice card.
KSEF_HowTo_Pay=Payments: which tool when
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Desc=The statement shows a different amount from the invoice: fees, commissions, bank rate, overpayment
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Intro=When the statement shows a different amount from the invoice, pick the Dolibarr tool by what happened:
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Short=<b>The invoice is not paid in full</b> and the rest will not come (a bank or operator deducted a fee, the bank converted at its own rate, another reason): enter a payment for the statement amount, then "%s" with a reason, e.g. "%s" or "%s", and a comment. Closing does not change VAT.
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_ShortAccount=With the Accounting module on, the window also asks for the account of the missing PLN amount; the entry goes to the "%s" journal (customer: debit this account, credit the customer; supplier: debit the supplier, credit this account). "%s" on the invoice removes that entry while it is not in the ledger.
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Extra=<b>The statement shows money beyond the invoice</b> (our own bank's fee on top of the transfer, a gain on the rate): enter a plain payment for the invoice amount, and enter the rest when reconciling the statement with the "%s" button (menu Banks > "%s").
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Over=<b>The customer paid more than the invoice</b>: enter a payment for the whole amount on the statement, then "%s" on the invoice card. The overpayment stays as the customer's credit: use it on a later invoice or pay it back. When you paid a supplier too much: "%s" on their invoice.
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_PayLater=<b>The rest comes later</b> (or you pay the supplier the rest later): leave the invoice open and enter another plain payment with the "%s" button when the money moves.
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Discount=<b>A discount after the sale</b>: issue a corrective invoice with the "%s" button on the invoice card; a supplier sends you its corrective invoice. Closing with a reason does not change VAT, so the close window has no "discount" reason.
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Eur=EUR account: the card of a payment on a currency account shows "%s": the value at the invoice rate and at the NBP rate of the last working day before the payment date. Dolibarr does not book that difference; enter it in the books by hand. A "%s" entry on a EUR account is booked by Dolibarr without conversion (the EUR amount as złoty): enter such a fee on a PLN account or correct the amount in the books.
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Mpp=Split payment (MPP): the money arrives on two accounts (main and VAT), so enter two plain payments, one per account.
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Accountant=The module does not compute or book: exchange differences on own funds of a currency account, year-end valuation, bad-debt relief, or payment operator invoices for commission; you enter those in the books by hand. Watch for a double cost: if you close an invoice that is short by the operator's fee with a reason booked to a cost account, and also book the operator's invoice for that fee as a cost, the cost is counted twice. In that case pick the operator's settlement account instead of a cost account when closing: the operator's invoice (debit cost, credit the operator's settlement account) then clears that balance.
KSEF_HowTo_Pay_Settings=Chart of accounts and loading it (CSV or JPK_KR_PD): Accounting > Setup > Chart of accounts
KSEF_Tour_UpdateHowTo=How to do this?
KSEF_Tour_update_apply=Applying a module update
KSEF_Tour_update_apply_Desc=After uploading a new version: run the database changes.
KSEF_Tour_update_apply_apply=The new module files are in place, but the database changes are not applied yet. Click "Apply update": the module makes a backup and runs the database changes without switching the module off.
KSEF_Tour_update_apply_confirm=Click "Yes". Settings, KSeF login data and the module's records stay.
KSEF_Tour_update_apply_done=Done: the database check below ran after the update and shows the state after it. The banner on the module pages goes away.
KSEF_Tour_Track_maint=Maintenance
