KSEF_Tour_Form_standard=Invoice form: the type "Standard invoice" is already selected. Check "Invoice date" (the issue date), "Payment terms", "Payment method" and "%s": KSeF gets the payment due date, method and bank account from them. Empty payment fields are filled with the defaults from the KSeF settings.
KSEF_Tour_Form_standard_nobank=Invoice form: the type "Standard invoice" is already selected. Check "Invoice date" (the issue date), "Payment terms" and "Payment method": KSeF gets the payment due date and method from them. There is no bank account field (Banks module off or no account), so the invoice goes to KSeF without a bank account.
KSEF_Tour_Form_deposit=Deposit form: check "Invoice date", "Payment terms", "Payment method" and "%s": KSeF gets the payment due date, method and bank account from them. Empty payment fields are filled with the defaults from the KSeF settings. Leave "Sale date" empty: the module takes the date the deposit was received from the payment.
KSEF_Tour_Form_deposit_nobank=Deposit form: check "Invoice date", "Payment terms" and "Payment method": KSeF gets the payment due date and method from them. There is no bank account field (Banks module off or no account), so the invoice goes to KSeF without a bank account. Leave "Sale date" empty: the module takes the date the deposit was received from the payment.
KSEF_Tour_FormCurrency=Currency: an invoice from an order already has the order's currency, keep it. Without an order, choose a foreign currency in the "Currency" field; the module takes the NBP rate as set in the KSeF settings. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_FormCurrency_noorder=Currency: choose a foreign currency in the "Currency" field; the module takes the NBP rate as set in the KSeF settings. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_FormCurrencyOff=The invoice will be in zloty. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_FormCurrencyMain=Note: the company's main currency in Dolibarr is not PLN, and without the Multicurrency module the invoice is in the main currency. Set "Main currency" to PLN in the company settings or switch on the Multicurrency module (link below). Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_FormCurrencyNext=You check the invoice currency in the next step. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_currency=Invoice currency: for an invoice in zloty keep PLN, for an invoice in a foreign currency choose it in the "Currency" field (e.g. EUR). The module takes the NBP rate as set in the KSeF settings. Then click "OK".
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_currency_preset=The invoice currency is set already (e.g. from the customer card). Keep it or change it in the "Currency" field; for an invoice in zloty choose PLN. The module takes the NBP rate as set in the KSeF settings. Then click "OK".
KSEF_Tour_SideModule=Module list: click the framed switch to turn the module on. Then click "Go back": the guide returns to the previous page and goes on.
KSEF_Tour_SideModuleOn=The module is on. Click "Go back": the guide returns to the previous page and goes on.
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_addrow=New line. %s
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_addrow=Check the deposit line in the framed row (description, type, VAT rate, gross amount) and click "Add".
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_line=Deposit line. In the framed row type the description and choose the type, Product or Service. Choose the VAT rate of the sale the deposit is for and type the gross amount received in "Unit price (inc. tax)". A deposit for lines at different rates: one line per rate. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_AddrowLine=In the framed row choose a product or service in "Predefined products or services" or type the description of a line not on the list and choose its type, Product or Service. Check "VAT rate", "Unit price (net)" and "Quantity", then click "Add".
KSEF_Tour_AddrowLine_noprod=In the framed row type the description and choose the type, Product or Service. Check "VAT rate", "Unit price (net)" and "Quantity", then click "Add".
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_addrow=Settlement invoice lines: add the lines of the whole sale at their full value excl. VAT, not reduced by the deposit. %s You deduct the deposits in the next stage.
KSEF_Tour_AddrowUnit=Check the unit too (e.g. "Piece"): it goes to KSeF as the line's measure.
KSEF_Tour_AddrowUnit_nosend=The unit stays on the invoice in Dolibarr; it goes to KSeF only after you switch on "Include the unit of measure" in the KSeF settings (tab "Outgoing: fields").
KSEF_Tour_send_vat_more=The lines are on the invoice. Check the amounts; you add another line in the row below the list.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_more=The deposit line is on the invoice; its gross amount is the deposit received.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_more=The invoice lines came over from the order. Check that this is the full value of the sale; you deduct the deposits in the next stage.
KSEF_Tour_send_roz_more_noorder=The invoice lines are listed. Check that this is the full value of the sale, not reduced by the deposit; you deduct the deposits in the next stage.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay=Pay a deposit
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_Desc=Payment of a deposit and marking it as available credit; then you settle it with a settlement invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_deposit=The list shows deposits accepted by KSeF in the current environment that have not been deducted on another invoice yet. Under each deposit number are its order and payment state. Click the number of the deposit you are paying.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_pay=This deposit is not paid yet. Click "Enter payment".
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_payform=Amount: in the row of deposit {ref} type the payment amount (the arrow next to it fills in the amount left to pay). When other customer invoices are listed, leave their amount fields empty. Then click the framed "Pay" button.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_payhead=Payment form, top: type the payment "Date" (or click "Now"), choose the "Payment method" and "%s". Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_payhead_nobank=Payment form, top: type the payment "Date" (or click "Now") and choose the "Payment method". There is no account field because the Banks module is off. Then click Next.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_payconfirm=Check the amount, leave "Yes" and click "Confirm". Dolibarr records the payment and returns to the deposit card.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_payconfirm_back=Check the amount, leave "Yes" and click "Confirm". Dolibarr records the payment and returns to the settlement invoice; the guide goes back there to the deposits step.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_done=Deposit paid and marked as available credit: the card status at the top right says it is ready to be used on the final invoice. Now you deduct it on the settlement invoice.
KSEF_Tour_send_zal_pay_done_back=The deposit is paid and is available credit. Click the invoice number in the "Settlement invoice" row: the guide "Settlement (final) invoice" goes back there to the deposits step.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_way_new=New backdated invoice
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_customer=A new invoice to practise offline mode: choose the customer (type a few letters of the name or the NIP). The page reloads after the choice.
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_backdate=Enter a date earlier than today in "Invoice date" (e.g. yesterday). The module offers to issue such an invoice offline. Then click "OK".
KSEF_Tour_send_offline_save=Click "Create draft". The guide goes on on the invoice card.
KSEF_Tour_recv_deposits_payform=Amount: in the row of this invoice type the payment amount in the invoice currency (the arrow next to it fills in the amount left to pay). When other supplier invoices are listed, leave their fields empty. Then click the framed "Pay" button.
KSEF_Tour_setup_incoming_jobs_off=The module's scheduled jobs and their state. The required jobs are still off: click "Enable the required jobs" in their row, and the guide goes on.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_lines_editing_roz=Settlement invoice correction: in the row being edited, enter the values after the correction, not the difference: "Qty" and "Unit price (net)". You do not change the deducted deposit row: the module deducts the deposit at its current value.
KSEF_Tour_send_kor_zal_send_roz=Click "Validate and send to KSeF". A settlement correction deducts the deposit at its current value; if the deposit changes while the correction is a draft, validation updates it. The module first shows its confirmation window, unless "Confirmation before uploading to KSeF" is switched off in the settings.
